{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XiXUHYFaGHUq9puCz9eCJo","type":"tool_result","content":"## B12 Prompt, CODEOWNERS and CI deploy controls look sound, but branch-protection settings are not in code. [] [] [{'file': 'src/agent.py', 'line': 28, 'note': 'System prompt and config load from files baked into the reviewed image.'}]\n   B12.1 unknown src/agent.py:28 [challenge: unclear] Prompt is read from a file baked into the image at build; config loaded from config/ via tools.py:14. No rules files (manifest rules_files: []). Type-id over src/, prompts/, config/ verified at startup (main.py:46). No DB/URL/flag override of prompt found.\n      COV not_applicable rules files (CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md) release/manifest.yaml:35 none exist\n   B12.2 unknown CODEOWNERS:2 [challenge: unclear] Prompts, config, src (via * and gateway/approvals specific), release, k8s, workflows and CODEOWNERS all matched. Enforcement of code-owner review itself is a repo setting not visible, but the CODEOWNERS coverage requirement is met.\n   B12.3 unknown .github/workflows/release.yml:5 [challenge: unclear] Only trigger is push to main, no workflow_dispatch; image tagged by sha, digest and git_sha stamped into manifest, deployed by digest; Kyverno admits only images signed by this workflow from main. No manual deploy scripts found.\n   B12.4 unknown .github/workflows/release.yml:5 [coverage] only matches are release.yml trigger and unrelated text\n      COV unclear main branch force-push/deletion protection .github/workflows/release.yml:5 main is named as source branch but no protection config found\n## A03 The type ID is a canonical SHA-256 over the image digest, model record and every file in src, prompts and config plus requirements and Dockerfile. ['Compute the agent-type-id as a hash of the container digest, harness, system prompt, model ID and version, and configuration. The model part includes checkpoint and fine-tune or adapter references where they apply. Keep the list of inputs (the manifest) and the hashing steps. Check that changing any input changes the ID, and that the same manifest gives the same ID.'] ['Dockerfile:12 not hashed, but not in image and not read by any code'] [{'file': 'src/type_id.py', 'line': 42, 'note': 'Manifest has image digest, model record, and hashes of src, prompts, config, requirements, Dockerfile.'}]\n   A03.1 unknown src/type_id.py:42 [challenge: unclear] SHA-256 over canonical manifest: image digest, model record (provider,id,pinning,adapter), per-file hashes of src/ (harness), prompts/ (system prompt), config/, requirements.txt, Dockerfile. CI computes it (release.yml:48) and pod verifies at start (main.py:46).\n   A03.2 no Dockerfile:12 [coverage] not hashed, but not in image and not read by any code\n      COV not_applicable .mcp.json (root, unhashed) .mcp.json:1 not copied by Dockerfile COPY lines (agent/Dockerfile:12-15), unreferenced in repo; not part of the runtime image\n   A03.3 unknown config/agent.yaml:10 [challenge: unclear] Model ID is a dated snapshot, read from config with no env var or default fallback; agent.py:71 uses the same model['id']. adapter: none is in the record, so adapters are hashed if ever used. No checkpoint/fine-tune used (manifest.yaml fine_tune: none).\n   A03.4 unknown src/type_id.py:43 [challenge: unclear] Sorted keys, compact separators, UTF-8 bytes; file list iterated via sorted() rglob and stored in dict that is key-sorted anyway; paths POSIX relative; files hashed as raw bytes so no line-ending normalisation variance.\n   A03.5 unknown src/type_id.py:30 [challenge: unclear] Manifest holds a scheme string, digest, model record and SHA-256 hashes of files, not file contents; no environment dump. Hashed config files contain no secrets (credentials come from env/STS at runtime). Stored type-id.json therefore exposes no secret values.\n## E04 N/A claim was not upheld: Agent loads external HRIS/helpdesk MCP servers, so N/A does not hold; no metad