{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChG5wvFNtvNjeNB9w4BTK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RJmSYwKawMBKQ87TEiaZig","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-action-_pgwuimk/scratch/make_fixes.py","content":"\"\"\"Adds components, fix and assignee to gap / needs_evidence findings. Touches nothing else.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport sys\n\nAGENT = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])\nTRIAL = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[2])\nPYTEST = \"python -m pytest \"\n\n\ndef test_of(name):\n    return {\"file\": f\"tests/{name}\", \"code\": (TRIAL / \"tests\" / name).read_text(), \"run\": PYTEST + f\"tests/{name}\"}\n\n\nDR = [\"tool:escalate_to_human\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\", \"mcp:helpdesk\"]\nGW = [\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"]\nRET = [\"tool:search_policies\", \"data:hr-postgres\"]\nAPPR = [\"tool:file_leave_request\", \"tool:escalate_to_human\"]\nAUD = [\"data:audit-log\"]\nLOOP = [\"unit:src/agent.py\"]\nALL = [\"agent\"]\n\nF = {}\n\n\ndef add(item, comps, problem, steps, done, effort, test=None):\n    F[item] = {\"components\": comps, \"fix\": {\"problem\": problem, \"steps\": steps, \"done_when\": done, \"effort\": effort}}\n    if test:\n        F[item][\"fix\"][\"test\"] = test\n\n\nDO_B01 = \"Do B01 first. It removes the direct route to the helpdesk server.\"\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Build time\nadd(\"B01\", DR,\n    \"If the gateway returns 503, `escalate_to_human` sends the call straight to the helpdesk server. That skips the gateway allowlist and stop checks.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests`. Create the file `tests/test_direct_route.py` from the test below. It fails until the next steps are done.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway_client.py`, replace lines 46 to 59 (the `try` and the whole `except GatewayUnavailable` block) with the two statements shown after this list, indented 8 spaces.\",\n     \"The first statement is `token = await self._creds.token(audience=GATEWAY_AUDIENCE, scope=spec.scope, subject_token=subject_token, subject=ctx.subject)`.\",\n     \"The second statement is `return await self._post(GATEWAY_URL, token, spec, args, ctx, operation_id)`.\",\n     \"In `config/tools.yaml`, delete lines 91 to 93. These are the `direct_route:` key and its `endpoint` and `audience` lines.\",\n     \"In `k8s/networkpolicy.yaml`, delete lines 48 to 50. This is the rule that lets the agent reach `helpdesk-mcp`. Keep the gateway rule at lines 76 to 79.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_direct_route.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"When the gateway returns 503, `escalate_to_human` fails and no request goes to the helpdesk server.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_direct_route.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B02\", RET + [\"agent\"],\n    \"The handbook search cache is keyed by query text only. One employee can be served another employee's private handbook chunks.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_retrieval_cache.py` from the test below. It fails until the next steps are done.\",\n     \"In `src/retrieval.py`, change line 46 to `key = self._key(query, employee_id)`. Do this before the next step, because it is lower in the file.\",\n     \"In `src/retrieval.py`, replace lines 40 to 42 with a `_key(self, query: str, employee_id: str)` method that keeps the `normalized` line.\",\n     \"Make that method end with `return hashlib.sha256(f\\\"{self._top_k}|{employee_id}|{normalized}\\\".encode()).hexdigest()`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_retrieval_cache.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"Ask the identity team to send you the STS scope policy and the HRIS and helpdesk audience rules, and keep them with the review record.\"],\n    \"Two employees who search the same words each get their own results, never the other's cached chunks.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_retrieval_cache.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B03\", [\"agent\", \"data:hr-postgres\"],\n    \"The database passwords and the Anthropic key are fixed secrets in `k8s/deployment.yaml`. No rotation or expiry is shown in the repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the platform team for the rotation schedule of the secrets `hr-agent-db`, `hr-gateway-db` and `hr-agent-anthropic`. Ask who owns each.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team whether the database accepts short-lived logins instead of a fixed password. Ask for the answer in writing.\",\n     \"Ask the identity team to confirm that tokens for the helpdesk and HRIS servers carry a `cnf` certificate binding.\",\n     \"Save the answers in `docs/credential-evidence.md`, and create that file. Give each secret an owner, a rotation date and a next review date.\",\n     \"Check that every secret named in `k8s/deployment.yaml` appears in that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/credential-evidence.md` lists every secret with an owner, a rotation period and the last rotation date.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"B04\", DR,\n    \"A stop flag does not reach every path. The direct helpdesk route skips the gateway stop check, and the gateway ignores `agent_type` flags.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Ask the identity team to add a signed claim named `agent_type_id` to the tokens that the gateway accepts. Do not deploy step 3 until they have shipped it.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, change line 84 so the `require` list also contains `\\\"agent_type_id\\\"`. Do this after step 4, because it is higher in the file.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, replace lines 101 and 102 so the query also has `OR (scope = 'agent_type' AND value = $4)` and the arguments end with `claims[\\\"agent_type_id\\\"]`.\",\n     \"Create the test below as `tests/test_gateway_stop.py`. Run `python -m pytest tests/test_gateway_stop.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"Write in `README.md` under \\\"Stopping the agent\\\" that tokens last up to 300 seconds and a stop flag is checked on every call.\"],\n    \"A stop flag with scope `agent_type` makes the gateway refuse that agent type's calls.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_gateway_stop.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B05\", APPR,\n    \"The approval text for a leave request leaves out the `note` the model wrote. The employee approves arguments they were never shown.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_approval_text.py` from the test below. One test fails until the next step is done.\",\n     \"In `src/approvals.py`, replace lines 30 to 32 so the leave text is stored in a variable named `text`.\",\n     \"After that, add `if args.get(\\\"note\\\"):` and, inside it, `text += f\\\" Your note to the manager: \\\\\\\"{args['note']}\\\\\\\"\\\"`. Then add `return text`. Keep all of it inside the first `if`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_approval_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The approval text for a leave request shows the note that will be sent.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_approval_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B06\", APPR,\n    \"The reviewer sees the leave type and dates but not the `note`, even though the approval hash covers the note.\",\n    [\"Do B05 first. It adds the note to `describe()` in `src/approvals.py`.\",\n     \"Open `describe()` in `src/approvals.py`. Check that every key in `input_schema` for each tool in `config/tools.yaml` appears in its text.\",\n     \"If you add a field to a tool later, add it to `describe()` in the same change.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_approval_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The text an employee approves contains every argument that is sent, including the note.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_approval_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B07\", [\"agent\", \"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n    \"The Anthropic client retries once on its own and only the last answer is counted. Concurrent runs can also pass the quota before it is recorded.\",\n    [\"In `src/main.py`, change line 172 from `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=1)` to `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=0)`. A failed call now fails once and is counted.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_budget_concurrency.py`. Make it start 30 calls to `QuotaStore.reserve_run` at once against a test database with a limit of 20 runs.\",\n     \"In that test, assert that exactly 20 calls succeed and 10 raise `BudgetExceeded`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_budget_concurrency.py`. Ask the platform team to run it against a real Postgres, because the repository has no test database.\"],\n    \"No more runs start than the quota allows, and a failed model call is not retried out of sight.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"B08\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The network and runtime files look correct, but nothing shows that they work in a running cluster.\",\n    [\"Ask the platform team to run a pod with the agent's labels in `hr-agent` and try to reach a public site. It should fail.\",\n     \"Ask them to try `169.254.169.254` from the same pod. It should fail too.\",\n     \"Ask them to try `hris-mcp` directly from the agent pod. It should fail, since only the gateway may reach it.\",\n     \"Save the commands, the dates and the results in `docs/egress-test.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/egress-test.md` shows a dated test where a public site, the metadata address and `hris-mcp` were all refused.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"B09\", DR,\n    \"The agent pod can reach the helpdesk server directly, and the client uses that path when the gateway is down.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Check that `k8s/networkpolicy.yaml` no longer has the `helpdesk-mcp` rule in the `hr-helpdesk-agent-egress` policy.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to try a call from the agent pod to `helpdesk-mcp` on port 8443. It must be refused.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_direct_route.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The agent pod cannot open a connection to `helpdesk-mcp`; only the gateway can.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"B10\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"Admission does not deny images that match no signing rule. The `platform/*` rule also checks no build attestation.\",\n    [\"In `k8s/admission.yaml`, add a rule after line 81 named `deny-unverified-images`, indented 4 spaces like the other rules.\",\n     \"Make that rule match Pods in `hr-agent` and use a `validate` block with a `deny` condition for any image that does not start with `registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent` or `registry.acme.example/platform/`.\",\n     \"Under the `platform/*` entry at line 72, add an `attestations` block like lines 51 to 71. Ask the platform team which build file to name.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to try a test pod with `registry.acme.example/other/app@sha256:...` in `hr-agent`. It must be refused.\"],\n    \"A pod in `hr-agent` with an image outside the two approved paths is refused by admission.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"B11\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The audit CronJob uses the `platform/psql` image. Its contents cannot be seen in this repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the platform team for the file list or SBOM of `registry.acme.example/platform/psql` at the digest in `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml` line 26.\",\n     \"Check the list for a shell, `curl`, `wget` and a package manager.\",\n     \"If any is present, ask the platform team to build a smaller image and put its new digest on line 26.\",\n     \"Save the SBOM and your check in `docs/psql-image-check.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/psql-image-check.md` shows the image has no shell, downloader or package manager.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"B12\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"Review rules for the `main` branch are repository settings. They are not in the code, so force-push and delete rules cannot be seen.\",\n    [\"Ask the repository admin to export the ruleset for `main` from the GitHub settings page.\",\n     \"Check that it blocks force-pushes and deletion and that it requires review by the code owners in `CODEOWNERS`.\",\n     \"Check that only the `release.yml` workflow can deploy, and that nobody can start it by hand.\",\n     \"Save the export in `docs/branch-protection.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/branch-protection.md` shows force-push and delete are blocked on `main` and code-owner review is required.\",\n    \"small\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Run time\nERR_STEP = (\"In `src/agent.py`, find the line `return _tool_result(tool_use_id, f\\\"{spec.name} failed: {exc.detail}\\\", error=True)` (line 188). \"\n            \"Change the text to `f\\\"{spec.name} failed. The details were recorded for review.\\\"`.\")\n\nadd(\"R01\", LOOP,\n    \"Error text from tools and the gateway goes to the model without any check on its size, content or safety.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_error_text.py` from the test below.\",\n     ERR_STEP,\n     \"The audit row at lines 184 to 186 already keeps the detail for people, so leave that code as it is.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_error_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"When a tool fails, the text sent to the model is a fixed message and never the server's error body.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_error_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R02\", LOOP,\n    \"Error text from tools reaches the model with no source or trust label, unlike results that succeed.\",\n    [\"Do R01 first. It replaces the error text with a fixed message, so no server text is left to label.\",\n     \"If you want the server's text kept, wrap it as `json.dumps({\\\"source\\\": spec.qualified, \\\"trust\\\": \\\"untrusted_data\\\", \\\"data\\\": ...})` like line 195.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_error_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"No text from a server reaches the model without the `untrusted_data` label or removal.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_error_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R03\", LOOP + [\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n    \"Error text reaches the model unredacted, and the approval text sent to the employee skips the link and image cleaner.\",\n    [\"Do R01 first. It fixes the error text at `src/agent.py` line 188.\",\n     \"In `src/main.py`, replace line 106 `body[\\\"approval\\\"] = state.pending_approval` with a copy whose `description` is cleaned.\",\n     \"The copy is `{**state.pending_approval, \\\"description\\\": sanitize_reply(state.pending_approval[\\\"description\\\"], CFG[\\\"output\\\"][\\\"allowed_link_hosts\\\"])}`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_approval_links.py`. Make it call `sanitize_reply` on a description with `![x](https://evil.example/a.png)` and assert `evil.example` is gone.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_approval_links.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"An approval text with an outside link or image shows no link or image to the employee.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"R04\", RET,\n    \"The search cache is keyed by query only, so one employee's private HR chunks can be returned to another.\",\n    [\"Do B02 first. It adds the employee id to the cache key in `src/retrieval.py`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_retrieval_cache.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"A second employee who repeats a query gets a fresh, filtered search and not the first employee's cached chunks.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_retrieval_cache.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R07\", LOOP + AUD,\n    \"Only the model-call audit row holds the context size. Tool rows and gateway rows drop it.\",\n    [\"Do not deploy the gateway change until the data-platform team has run step 2 on the database.\",\n     \"Create `migrations/002_context_tokens.sql` with `ALTER TABLE audit.gateway_decisions ADD COLUMN context_tokens integer;`. Ask the data-platform team to run it.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, after line 76, add `state.extra[\\\"context_tokens\\\"] = ctx_tokens`, indented 16 spaces.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, at lines 100, 103, 110, 115, 120, 174, 180, 184, 190 and 193, add `context_tokens=state.extra.get(\\\"context_tokens\\\")` to each `self.audit.record(` call.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway_client.py`, add the header `\\\"X-Context-Tokens\\\"` in `_post` and pass the value in. In `src/gateway.py` `_log`, store it in the new column.\",\n     \"Run a chat that uses a tool. In `audit.events`, check that the `tool_result` row has `context_tokens` set.\"],\n    \"Every tool action row in `audit.events` has `context_tokens` set, and so does its gateway row.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"R08\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No security detection rules or alert routing are in the repository. They may live in another system.\",\n    [\"Ask the security team for the rules that watch `run_stopped`, `tool_denied`, `approval_rejected`, `quota_denied` and `content_held` events.\",\n     \"Ask them to show who gets each alert and how fast.\",\n     \"Ask them to cause a test event of each kind in a test cluster and show that the alert arrived.\",\n     \"Save the rules and the test alert times in `docs/detection-evidence.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/detection-evidence.md` shows a test alert for each of the five event types reaching a named responder.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"R09\", [\"agent\", \"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n    \"Only fixed per-run limits exist. Nothing looks at chains of actions or adjusts limits for the size of the context.\",\n    [\"Ask the security team where chain rules can run, for example on the `audit.events` table. Ask who answers alerts.\",\n     \"Write down two chains to catch: a read of private data followed by `escalate_to_human`, and three denials in one run.\",\n     \"Create `docs/detection-rules.md` with the chains, the thresholds and the alert owner. Ask the security team to build the rules.\",\n     \"Ask them to replay a recorded run with each chain and show that the alert fires.\"],\n    \"`docs/detection-rules.md` lists the chains with thresholds, and a replayed run triggers each alert.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"R10\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No reviewer checks the agent's actions for misaligned behaviour, and no record says this risk is out of scope.\",\n    [\"Ask the business owner and the security lead to decide whether misaligned behaviour is in scope. Write the decision in `docs/misalignment-scope.md`.\",\n     \"If it is in scope, ask the model team to design a second reviewer that sees actions but not the untrusted text.\",\n     \"Ask them to build 20 labelled test traces, some evasive, and measure how many the reviewer misses.\",\n     \"Add the miss rate and the date to `docs/misalignment-scope.md`.\"],\n    \"`docs/misalignment-scope.md` holds a dated decision and, if in scope, the measured miss rate.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"R11\", DR,\n    \"The direct helpdesk route skips the gateway stop check, and the repository has no dated stop drill.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"In a test cluster, set a `fleet` flag in `control.stop_flags`. Check that a new chat and a tool call are both refused within 10 seconds. That limit is `max_stop_seconds` in `config/agent.yaml` line 51.\",\n     \"Repeat the drill with one flag each for `agent_instance`, `subject`, `agent_principal` and `agent_type`. Do the last one after B04.\",\n     \"Create `docs/stop-drill.md`. Write the date, who ran it, each scope tested, the seconds taken and the result.\",\n     \"Ask the operations lead to set a drill every three months and to review `docs/stop-drill.md`.\"],\n    \"`docs/stop-drill.md` shows a dated drill where every stop scope stopped the agent in 10 seconds.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"R12\", LOOP + [\"tool:file_leave_request\", \"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n    \"No stop rule says what happens to a leave request or ticket that was running when the agent stopped. Unknown outcomes are not held.\",\n    [\"Do R13 first. It records a row when a call is cancelled.\",\n     \"In `config/tools.yaml`, add `on_stop: complete_or_reconcile` to `file_leave_request` and `escalate_to_human`, and `on_stop: cancel` to the read tools.\",\n     \"In `src/tools.py`, add the field `on_stop: str = \\\"cancel\\\"` to `ToolSpec` and read it in `__init__` at line 47 with `on_stop=t.get(\\\"on_stop\\\", \\\"cancel\\\")`.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, in the `tool_outcome_unknown` handler from R13, write the `operation_id` into the audit row's `result`.\",\n     \"Ask the operations lead for a named owner who checks each `tool_outcome_unknown` row against HRIS and the helpdesk, and writes the result down.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_audit_steps.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"Every `tool_outcome_unknown` audit row has an operation id and a named owner who checks it.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_audit_steps.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R13\", LOOP,\n    \"The balance re-check call and cancelled tool calls leave no audit step. The direct retry also leaves none.\",\n    [\"Do B01 first. It removes the direct retry.\",\n     \"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_audit_steps.py` from the test below.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, after line 192 add `except asyncio.CancelledError:` at 12 spaces indent. Inside it add an `await self.audit.record(...)` for `\\\"tool_outcome_unknown\\\"` and then `raise`.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, replace lines 149 to 159 with a `_recheck_state` that takes `parent_step_id` and calls `self.audit.record` for `proposed_action` before and `tool_result` after the gateway call.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, change line 134 to call `self._recheck_state(ctx, state, spec, args, step_id)`.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, add `import asyncio` on the line before `import json` at line 4.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_audit_steps.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The balance re-check and a cancelled tool call each leave an audit row linked to the step.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_audit_steps.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R14\", [\"data:audit-log\", \"data:hr-postgres\", \"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n    \"Approval and audit rows are plain rows that anyone with write access could change. A gateway 503 also causes an automatic resend.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to export `audit.events` and `approvals.grants` every day to storage that cannot be changed, such as object lock.\",\n     \"In `src/approvals.py`, add a column `row_sha256` to the insert at line 46 that hashes `approval_id`, `operation`, `target`, `args_sha256` and `expires_at`.\",\n     \"In `pending()` at line 88, recompute that hash and raise `ApprovalInvalid` if it differs.\",\n     \"Create `migrations/003_grant_hash.sql` with `ALTER TABLE approvals.grants ADD COLUMN row_sha256 char(64);`. Ask the data-platform team to run it first.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_grant_hash.py` that changes a stored `args` value and checks `pending()` refuses it, then run it.\"],\n    \"A changed approval row is refused at resume, and daily exports of audit and approval rows exist.\",\n    \"large\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Agent\nadd(\"A01\", [\"agent\", \"api:sts\"],\n    \"The code gives the agent its own identity. Whether only that identity can be revoked is decided in systems outside this repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the identity team for the STS policy that issues tokens to `spiffe://acme.example/ns/hr-agent/sa/hr-helpdesk-agent`.\",\n     \"Ask them to revoke only that identity in a test cluster and show that employees' own logins still work.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to show that the database role `hr_agent` can be locked without touching `hr_gateway`.\",\n     \"Save the policy and the drill results in `docs/identity-evidence.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/identity-evidence.md` shows a dated drill that revoked only the agent identity.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"A02\", [\"agent\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\", \"data:audit-log\"],\n    \"Requests that fail sign-in are not audited at the agent. In the gateway they are logged with `unknown` identity fields.\",\n    [\"In `src/main.py`, in `chat` at line 113 and in `confirm` at line 139, add a `log.warning(\\\"unauthenticated request\\\", extra={\\\"path\\\": str(request.url.path)})` before each 401.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to add table `audit.preauth_denials` with `ts`, `path`, `peer` and `reason`. Then write one row there at both places.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, change `_log` so that a failed write raises instead of being skipped at line 196, and return 503.\",\n     \"Create `docs/audit-fields.md` listing which of the six fields each pre-sign-in row can fill, and why the others are `unknown`.\",\n     \"Send a bad token to `/v1/chat` in a test cluster. Check that one row appears in `audit.preauth_denials`.\"],\n    \"A request with a bad token leaves one audit row, and a failed audit write makes the gateway answer 503.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"A03\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"`.mcp.json` is not part of the type ID, so changing it does not change the agent's identity.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_type_id.py` from the test below.\",\n     \"In `src/type_id.py`, change line 21 to `INPUT_FILES = (\\\"requirements.txt\\\", \\\"Dockerfile\\\", \\\".mcp.json\\\")`.\",\n     \"In `Dockerfile`, change line 12 to `COPY --chown=0:0 requirements.txt Dockerfile .mcp.json ./`. The file must be in the image, or the pod stops at start.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_type_id.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"Make the same change to `README.md` line 60, which lists the inputs.\"],\n    \"Changing `.mcp.json` changes the agent type ID, and the same files give the same ID twice.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_type_id.py\"))\n\nadd(\"A04\", GW + [\"agent\"],\n    \"The gateway trusts an instance ID and a trace ID that the caller writes in a header. A resumed approval also starts a new trace.\",\n    [\"Ask the identity team to add the claim `agent_instance_id` to tokens. Do not deploy the next steps until they have shipped it.\",\n     \"In `src/credentials.py`, add `ctx` data to `token()` so the claim is requested, and add the instance to the cache key at line 42.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, at line 170, read `instance = claims[\\\"agent_instance_id\\\"]` instead of the header.\",\n     \"In `migrations/001_init.sql` line 54, add the column `traceparent text` to `approvals.grants`. Store it in `request()` and restore it in `resume_with_approval`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_gateway_instance.py`. Send a call with a header that differs from the claim, and assert the claim is used.\",\n     \"Run the new test with `python -m pytest tests/test_gateway_instance.py`.\"],\n    \"The gateway uses the instance ID from the signed token. A header value cannot change which flag or rate limit applies.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"A05\", GW + AUD,\n    \"A stop flag for one agent type is not enforced at the gateway. Gateway audit rows keep IDs that the caller supplied.\",\n    [\"Do B04 first. It adds the `agent_type` stop scope and a signed `agent_type_id`.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, in `_log` at lines 137 to 139, replace the two `request.headers.get(...)` values with `c.get(\\\"agent_type_id\\\")` and the verified instance.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to rename the columns at `migrations/001_init.sql` line 23 to `agent_type_id` and `agent_instance_id`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_gateway_stop.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"In a test cluster, call the gateway with a spoofed header. Check the audit row holds the token's value.\"],\n    \"A flag with scope `agent_type` stops calls at the gateway, and its audit rows hold the signed type ID.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_gateway_stop.py\"))\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Configuration\nadd(\"C01\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The release manifest leaves out the issuers, audiences, MCP versions, tool fingerprints and cache settings. Most entries have no owner.\",\n    [\"In `release/manifest.yaml`, add to `identity_bindings` after line 71 the keys `sso: {issuer: https://sso.acme.example, audience: hr-helpdesk}` and `sts: {issuer: https://sts.acme.example, audience: hr-tool-gateway}`.\",\n     \"Add a key `mcp_protocol` under `tools` with the version the gateway speaks. Ask the gateway owner for it.\",\n     \"Under each server at lines 54 and 55, add `fingerprints: config/tools.yaml` and a `settings` key naming the retrieval cache ttl `cache_ttl_seconds: 900`.\",\n     \"For `system_prompt`, `configuration`, `network` and `admission`, add an `owner` and a `ref` with the git commit or file digest.\",\n     \"Run `python -c \\\"import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('release/manifest.yaml'))\\\"` to check the file still loads.\"],\n    \"`release/manifest.yaml` has issuer and audience for both token services and an owner for every entry.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"C02\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"One catch-all code owner can change the Dockerfile, dependencies and most of `src/` alone. No emergency change path is written down.\",\n    [\"In `CODEOWNERS`, insert three lines after line 1: `/src/`, `/Dockerfile` and `/requirements.txt`. Give each `@acme/people-platform @acme/security-engineering`.\",\n     \"Keep line 4 (`/src/gateway.py`) and line 5 below them, because the last matching line wins.\",\n     \"Create `docs/emergency-change.md`. Write who may approve an urgent change, how it is recorded, and when review happens after it.\",\n     \"Ask the repository admin to confirm that code-owner review is required on `main`.\",\n     \"Open a test pull request that changes `Dockerfile`. Check that GitHub asks for `@acme/security-engineering`.\"],\n    \"A pull request that changes `Dockerfile`, `requirements.txt` or `src/` needs the security team to review it.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"C03\", [\"agent\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n    \"Only the agent checks its own identity at start. Nothing outside it compares the running prompt, model and tools to the approved manifest.\",\n    [\"Create `k8s/identity-check.yaml` with a CronJob that runs every 15 minutes in `hr-agent`. Ask the platform team which image it should use.\",\n     \"Make the job read the `AGENT_TYPE_ID` of each running pod, and compare it to `agent_type_id` in the stored manifest for that release.\",\n     \"Make the job send an alert to the security channel and set a stop flag of scope `agent_type` when they differ.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to run the job against a test pod with a changed prompt. Check that the alert fires.\"],\n    \"A pod whose type ID differs from the approved manifest causes an alert within 15 minutes.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"C04\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No check compares the running prompts, tools, permissions and network rules with the approved baseline.\",\n    [\"Do C03 first. It adds the scheduled job.\",\n     \"Extend that job to hash the live `NetworkPolicy`, the `ClusterPolicy` and `tools.yaml` and compare them to hashes in `release/manifest.yaml`.\",\n     \"In `config/agent.yaml`, add a `drift` block with `alert_channel`, `response: stop_agent_type` and `max_minutes: 15`.\",\n     \"Change one network rule in a test cluster. Check that the alert and the response happen within 15 minutes.\"],\n    \"A changed network rule or tool file in a test cluster triggers an alert and a stop within 15 minutes.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"C05\", [\"model:claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\"],\n    \"Nothing re-tests the hosted model on a schedule or watches for provider notices.\",\n    [\"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, add a new workflow `.github/workflows/model-retest.yml` with `on: schedule` set to weekly.\",\n     \"Make the new workflow run `python -m pytest -q tests/release`, the same tests as the release.\",\n     \"Ask the model team to subscribe to the Anthropic model deprecation notices and name an owner in `release/manifest.yaml` under `models.primary`.\",\n     \"Trigger the workflow by hand once and check that it runs the tests.\"],\n    \"A weekly job runs the release tests against the pinned model, and a named person watches provider notices.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"C06\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The release job runs tests in `tests/release`, but that folder does not exist. Results are not saved with the release.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests/release`. Create `tests/release/test_approval_text.py` from the test below, as a first case.\",\n     \"Add one test file for each of: denied destructive action, access limits, prompt injection, audit rows, stopping, retrieval and checkers.\",\n     \"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, change line 58 to a list of lines naming `type-id.json`, `release/manifest.yaml` and `test-results.xml`.\",\n     \"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, change line 29 to `python -m pytest -q tests/release --junitxml=test-results.xml`.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to add a job after `build` that runs the same tests inside the built image digest.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/release`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The release job runs real tests and uploads `test-results.xml` with the manifest.\",\n    \"large\", {\"file\": \"tests/release/test_approval_text.py\", \"code\": (TRIAL / \"tests/test_approval_text.py\").read_text(),\n              \"run\": PYTEST + \"tests/release/test_approval_text.py\"})\n\nadd(\"C07\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"There is no stored earlier release, rollback steps or model retirement date.\",\n    [\"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, add a `rollback` job after line 75 that takes an old `git_sha` and re-applies its stored manifest.\",\n     \"Keep each release's manifest by digest. Ask the platform team where to store them.\",\n     \"In `release/manifest.yaml` under `models.primary`, add `retirement_date` from the provider notice. Ask the model team for it.\",\n     \"Create `docs/rollback.md` saying how to drain pending approvals and discard the cached index on rollback.\",\n     \"Run the rollback job once in a test cluster. Check that the older version answers a chat.\"],\n    \"A tested rollback job exists and the manifest holds the model retirement date.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"C08\", GW + AUD,\n    \"Gateway rows cannot be tied to a stored release manifest, and audit rows are kept about six weeks instead of six months.\",\n    [\"Do E11 first. It fixes how long audit rows are kept.\",\n     \"Do A05 first. It stores a signed type ID in gateway rows.\",\n     \"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, upload the manifest under the name `manifest-<agent_type_id>` so it can be found by type ID.\",\n     \"In a test cluster, take one gateway row. Find its manifest using the stored type ID.\"],\n    \"From any gateway audit row you can find the exact release manifest by its type ID.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Ecosystem\nadd(\"E01\", [\"agent\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\", \"api:sts\"],\n    \"No inventory covers the gateway, token service, registry, audit store and stop service. Entries have only one owner.\",\n    [\"In `release/manifest.yaml`, add a `services` list after line 55.\",\n     \"Add an entry for the gateway, STS, JWKS, image registry, Postgres and the telemetry collector.\",\n     \"Give each entry `agent_team_owner` and `provider_owner`.\",\n     \"Run `python -c \\\"import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('release/manifest.yaml'))\\\"` to check the file loads.\"],\n    \"Every outside service the agent uses has two named owners in `release/manifest.yaml`.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"E02\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No scan for known weaknesses runs in CI, and there are no records about who publishes each dependency.\",\n    [\"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, add a step after line 28: `- run: pip install pip-audit && pip-audit -r requirements.txt --require-hashes`.\",\n     \"Create `docs/dependencies.md`. For each line in `requirements.txt`, write publisher, permissions and update source.\",\n     \"For `hris` and `helpdesk` in `config/tools.yaml`, add the publisher and update source next to `owner`.\",\n     \"Push a test branch. Check that the new step runs and the job fails when a known bad version is listed.\"],\n    \"The release job fails when a dependency has a known weakness, and every dependency has a record.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"E03\", DR,\n    \"Tool fingerprints are checked only every 300 seconds, a list change message is ignored, and a gateway error skips the check.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, call `refresh_fingerprints()` before the tool lookup at line 165, with a short time limit. Refuse the call if it fails.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py` line 213, lower the sleep from 300 to 60 seconds.\",\n     \"In `config/tools.yaml`, add `implementation_ref` with the server's image digest under `hris` and `helpdesk`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_fingerprint.py` that changes a live description and asserts the tool is disabled. Run it.\"],\n    \"A changed tool description disables the tool before the next call and not after five minutes.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E04\", GW + [\"tool:search_policies\"],\n    \"Server instructions, descriptions and schemas are only fingerprinted. They are never scanned for hidden instructions.\",\n    [\"In `src/gateway.py`, add `scan_metadata(tool)` that rejects zero-width and control characters, long strings and phrases like `ignore previous`.\",\n     \"Call it from `refresh_fingerprints` at line 64 for every live tool, and disable the tool when it fails.\",\n     \"Also fetch `initialize` server `instructions` and scan them the same way.\",\n     \"Add a unit test with a description holding a zero-width character. Assert the tool is disabled.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_metadata_scan.py`.\"],\n    \"A tool with hidden characters or override words in its metadata is disabled before the model sees it.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E05\", GW,\n    \"Lookalike tool names across servers are only logged. Tricks such as Cyrillic letters are not detected.\",\n    [\"In `src/gateway.py`, replace the `log.error` at line 67 with `_disabled.update(...)` for every tool in the clash.\",\n     \"At line 65, add a confusables map for Cyrillic and Greek letters before the `casefold()` call.\",\n     \"In `src/approvals.py`, add the server id to the approval text in `describe()`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_lookalike.py` with the names `create_ticket` and `create_tіcket` (Cyrillic i). Assert both are disabled. Run it.\"],\n    \"Two tools whose names look alike are both disabled and the clash is logged.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E06\", DR,\n    \"When the gateway returns 503 the client sends `escalate_to_human` straight to the helpdesk server and skips the gateway.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Check `.mcp.json` and `src/gateway_client.py` for any other URL that is not `GATEWAY_URL`. There should be none.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_direct_route.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The only network route to the helpdesk server goes through the gateway.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_direct_route.py\"))\n\nadd(\"E09\", DR + [\"api:sts\"],\n    \"A stop flag does not revoke tokens already issued. They last 300 seconds, and the direct route skips the stop check.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"In `src/credentials.py`, change line 20 from `300` to `60` so a stop is effective sooner.\",\n     \"In `src/credentials.py`, call `drop_subject` from `StopControl` when it cancels a run (`src/killswitch.py` line 58).\",\n     \"Ask the identity team for a revoke call. Call it for the subject when a stop flag appears.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, record in-flight tool calls at stop. R13 adds this record.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_audit_steps.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"After a stop, a copied token is refused within 60 seconds and every in-flight call has an audit row.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_audit_steps.py\"))\n\nadd(\"E10\", GW + DR,\n    \"Gateway audit rows lack verified identity and the vendor's receipt ID, and an allow row is written only after the action.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Do A05 first. It stores a signed type ID in gateway rows.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, at line 190, add the `request_id` or `ticket_id` from `structured` to the reason written by `_log`.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, write a `pending` row before line 177 and update it after line 190. Return 503 if the first write fails.\",\n     \"Run a ticket call in a test cluster. Check the `audit.gateway_decisions` row holds the ticket id.\"],\n    \"Every gateway call has a row written before it runs and holds the vendor receipt ID after.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E11\", AUD,\n    \"Audit rows are kept about six weeks, not six months. Nothing shows if rows are missing or changed.\",\n    [\"In `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`, change line 35 from `\\\"6\\\"` to `\\\"27\\\"`. That is 26 weeks plus a spare.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to add a `seq bigserial` column to `audit.events` and alert on gaps in it.\",\n     \"Ask them to export audit rows each day to storage that cannot be changed, and to alert if the export fails.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, write the audit row before forwarding the call. E10 covers this.\",\n     \"After the next night's run, ask the data-platform team to check that the oldest partition is about 26 weeks old.\"],\n    \"The oldest `audit.events` partition is at least 26 weeks old, and a gap in `seq` causes an alert.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E12\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No runbook, alert route, fleet impact query or outside-reporting owner is in the repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the security lead to write the runbook for an incident that affects every agent of this type, and create `docs/incident-runbook.md`.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team for a query that lists all runs and subjects touched by one agent type ID in a time range.\",\n     \"Name the person who decides on outside reporting in the runbook.\",\n     \"Run a drill: stop, quarantine and revoke the agent in a test cluster. Record the alert times in the runbook.\",\n     \"Check that `docs/incident-runbook.md` has the query, the owner, the alert times and the drill date.\"],\n    \"`docs/incident-runbook.md` holds a fleet impact query, a named reporting owner and a dated drill result.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\npath = AGENT / \"brace-findings.json\"\ndata = json.loads(path.read_text())\ncount = 0\nfor f in data[\"findings\"]:\n    if f[\"rating\"] in (\"gap\", \"needs_evidence\"):\n        entry = F.pop(f[\"item\"])\n        f[\"components\"] = entry[\"components\"]\n        f[\"fix\"] = entry[\"fix\"]\n        f[\"assignee\"] = None\n        count += 1\nassert not F, f\"unused fixes: {list(F)}\"\npath.write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\nprint(\"updated\", count)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":925,"cache_read_input_tokens":120833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":925},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"981bf4ba-51f4-44d7-811c-79f7b4ddcca3","uuid":"c9649441-9663-44e2-a2aa-b2e37093c2ea","timestamp":"2026-11-21T12:39:49.769Z","request_id":"req_011ChG5wv3iDA5BgeXTnAPwV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RJmSYwKawMBKQ87TEiaZig":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-action-_pgwuimk/scratch/make_fixes.py","content":"\"\"\"Adds components, fix and assignee to gap / needs_evidence findings. Touches nothing else.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport sys\n\nAGENT = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])\nTRIAL = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[2])\nPYTEST = \"python -m pytest \"\n\n\ndef test_of(name):\n    return {\"file\": f\"tests/{name}\", \"code\": (TRIAL / \"tests\" / name).read_text(), \"run\": PYTEST + f\"tests/{name}\"}\n\n\nDR = [\"tool:escalate_to_human\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\", \"mcp:helpdesk\"]\nGW = [\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"]\nRET = [\"tool:search_policies\", \"data:hr-postgres\"]\nAPPR = [\"tool:file_leave_request\", \"tool:escalate_to_human\"]\nAUD = [\"data:audit-log\"]\nLOOP = [\"unit:src/agent.py\"]\nALL = [\"agent\"]\n\nF = {}\n\n\ndef add(item, comps, problem, steps, done, effort, test=None):\n    F[item] = {\"components\": comps, \"fix\": {\"problem\": problem, \"steps\": steps, \"done_when\": done, \"effort\": effort}}\n    if test:\n        F[item][\"fix\"][\"test\"] = test\n\n\nDO_B01 = \"Do B01 first. It removes the direct route to the helpdesk server.\"\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Build time\nadd(\"B01\", DR,\n    \"If the gateway returns 503, `escalate_to_human` sends the call straight to the helpdesk server. That skips the gateway allowlist and stop checks.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests`. Create the file `tests/test_direct_route.py` from the test below. It fails until the next steps are done.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway_client.py`, replace lines 46 to 59 (the `try` and the whole `except GatewayUnavailable` block) with the two statements shown after this list, indented 8 spaces.\",\n     \"The first statement is `token = await self._creds.token(audience=GATEWAY_AUDIENCE, scope=spec.scope, subject_token=subject_token, subject=ctx.subject)`.\",\n     \"The second statement is `return await self._post(GATEWAY_URL, token, spec, args, ctx, operation_id)`.\",\n     \"In `config/tools.yaml`, delete lines 91 to 93. These are the `direct_route:` key and its `endpoint` and `audience` lines.\",\n     \"In `k8s/networkpolicy.yaml`, delete lines 48 to 50. This is the rule that lets the agent reach `helpdesk-mcp`. Keep the gateway rule at lines 76 to 79.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_direct_route.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"When the gateway returns 503, `escalate_to_human` fails and no request goes to the helpdesk server.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_direct_route.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B02\", RET + [\"agent\"],\n    \"The handbook search cache is keyed by query text only. One employee can be served another employee's private handbook chunks.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_retrieval_cache.py` from the test below. It fails until the next steps are done.\",\n     \"In `src/retrieval.py`, change line 46 to `key = self._key(query, employee_id)`. Do this before the next step, because it is lower in the file.\",\n     \"In `src/retrieval.py`, replace lines 40 to 42 with a `_key(self, query: str, employee_id: str)` method that keeps the `normalized` line.\",\n     \"Make that method end with `return hashlib.sha256(f\\\"{self._top_k}|{employee_id}|{normalized}\\\".encode()).hexdigest()`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_retrieval_cache.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"Ask the identity team to send you the STS scope policy and the HRIS and helpdesk audience rules, and keep them with the review record.\"],\n    \"Two employees who search the same words each get their own results, never the other's cached chunks.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_retrieval_cache.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B03\", [\"agent\", \"data:hr-postgres\"],\n    \"The database passwords and the Anthropic key are fixed secrets in `k8s/deployment.yaml`. No rotation or expiry is shown in the repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the platform team for the rotation schedule of the secrets `hr-agent-db`, `hr-gateway-db` and `hr-agent-anthropic`. Ask who owns each.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team whether the database accepts short-lived logins instead of a fixed password. Ask for the answer in writing.\",\n     \"Ask the identity team to confirm that tokens for the helpdesk and HRIS servers carry a `cnf` certificate binding.\",\n     \"Save the answers in `docs/credential-evidence.md`, and create that file. Give each secret an owner, a rotation date and a next review date.\",\n     \"Check that every secret named in `k8s/deployment.yaml` appears in that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/credential-evidence.md` lists every secret with an owner, a rotation period and the last rotation date.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"B04\", DR,\n    \"A stop flag does not reach every path. The direct helpdesk route skips the gateway stop check, and the gateway ignores `agent_type` flags.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Ask the identity team to add a signed claim named `agent_type_id` to the tokens that the gateway accepts. Do not deploy step 3 until they have shipped it.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, change line 84 so the `require` list also contains `\\\"agent_type_id\\\"`. Do this after step 4, because it is higher in the file.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, replace lines 101 and 102 so the query also has `OR (scope = 'agent_type' AND value = $4)` and the arguments end with `claims[\\\"agent_type_id\\\"]`.\",\n     \"Create the test below as `tests/test_gateway_stop.py`. Run `python -m pytest tests/test_gateway_stop.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"Write in `README.md` under \\\"Stopping the agent\\\" that tokens last up to 300 seconds and a stop flag is checked on every call.\"],\n    \"A stop flag with scope `agent_type` makes the gateway refuse that agent type's calls.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_gateway_stop.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B05\", APPR,\n    \"The approval text for a leave request leaves out the `note` the model wrote. The employee approves arguments they were never shown.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_approval_text.py` from the test below. One test fails until the next step is done.\",\n     \"In `src/approvals.py`, replace lines 30 to 32 so the leave text is stored in a variable named `text`.\",\n     \"After that, add `if args.get(\\\"note\\\"):` and, inside it, `text += f\\\" Your note to the manager: \\\\\\\"{args['note']}\\\\\\\"\\\"`. Then add `return text`. Keep all of it inside the first `if`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_approval_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The approval text for a leave request shows the note that will be sent.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_approval_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B06\", APPR,\n    \"The reviewer sees the leave type and dates but not the `note`, even though the approval hash covers the note.\",\n    [\"Do B05 first. It adds the note to `describe()` in `src/approvals.py`.\",\n     \"Open `describe()` in `src/approvals.py`. Check that every key in `input_schema` for each tool in `config/tools.yaml` appears in its text.\",\n     \"If you add a field to a tool later, add it to `describe()` in the same change.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_approval_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The text an employee approves contains every argument that is sent, including the note.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_approval_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B07\", [\"agent\", \"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n    \"The Anthropic client retries once on its own and only the last answer is counted. Concurrent runs can also pass the quota before it is recorded.\",\n    [\"In `src/main.py`, change line 172 from `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=1)` to `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=0)`. A failed call now fails once and is counted.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_budget_concurrency.py`. Make it start 30 calls to `QuotaStore.reserve_run` at once against a test database with a limit of 20 runs.\",\n     \"In that test, assert that exactly 20 calls succeed and 10 raise `BudgetExceeded`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_budget_concurrency.py`. Ask the platform team to run it against a real Postgres, because the repository has no test database.\"],\n    \"No more runs start than the quota allows, and a failed model call is not retried out of sight.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"B08\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The network and runtime files look correct, but nothing shows that they work in a running cluster.\",\n    [\"Ask the platform team to run a pod with the agent's labels in `hr-agent` and try to reach a public site. It should fail.\",\n     \"Ask them to try `169.254.169.254` from the same pod. It should fail too.\",\n     \"Ask them to try `hris-mcp` directly from the agent pod. It should fail, since only the gateway may reach it.\",\n     \"Save the commands, the dates and the results in `docs/egress-test.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/egress-test.md` shows a dated test where a public site, the metadata address and `hris-mcp` were all refused.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"B09\", DR,\n    \"The agent pod can reach the helpdesk server directly, and the client uses that path when the gateway is down.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Check that `k8s/networkpolicy.yaml` no longer has the `helpdesk-mcp` rule in the `hr-helpdesk-agent-egress` policy.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to try a call from the agent pod to `helpdesk-mcp` on port 8443. It must be refused.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_direct_route.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The agent pod cannot open a connection to `helpdesk-mcp`; only the gateway can.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"B10\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"Admission does not deny images that match no signing rule. The `platform/*` rule also checks no build attestation.\",\n    [\"In `k8s/admission.yaml`, add a rule after line 81 named `deny-unverified-images`, indented 4 spaces like the other rules.\",\n     \"Make that rule match Pods in `hr-agent` and use a `validate` block with a `deny` condition for any image that does not start with `registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent` or `registry.acme.example/platform/`.\",\n     \"Under the `platform/*` entry at line 72, add an `attestations` block like lines 51 to 71. Ask the platform team which build file to name.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to try a test pod with `registry.acme.example/other/app@sha256:...` in `hr-agent`. It must be refused.\"],\n    \"A pod in `hr-agent` with an image outside the two approved paths is refused by admission.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"B11\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The audit CronJob uses the `platform/psql` image. Its contents cannot be seen in this repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the platform team for the file list or SBOM of `registry.acme.example/platform/psql` at the digest in `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml` line 26.\",\n     \"Check the list for a shell, `curl`, `wget` and a package manager.\",\n     \"If any is present, ask the platform team to build a smaller image and put its new digest on line 26.\",\n     \"Save the SBOM and your check in `docs/psql-image-check.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/psql-image-check.md` shows the image has no shell, downloader or package manager.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"B12\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"Review rules for the `main` branch are repository settings. They are not in the code, so force-push and delete rules cannot be seen.\",\n    [\"Ask the repository admin to export the ruleset for `main` from the GitHub settings page.\",\n     \"Check that it blocks force-pushes and deletion and that it requires review by the code owners in `CODEOWNERS`.\",\n     \"Check that only the `release.yml` workflow can deploy, and that nobody can start it by hand.\",\n     \"Save the export in `docs/branch-protection.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/branch-protection.md` shows force-push and delete are blocked on `main` and code-owner review is required.\",\n    \"small\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Run time\nERR_STEP = (\"In `src/agent.py`, find the line `return _tool_result(tool_use_id, f\\\"{spec.name} failed: {exc.detail}\\\", error=True)` (line 188). \"\n            \"Change the text to `f\\\"{spec.name} failed. The details were recorded for review.\\\"`.\")\n\nadd(\"R01\", LOOP,\n    \"Error text from tools and the gateway goes to the model without any check on its size, content or safety.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_error_text.py` from the test below.\",\n     ERR_STEP,\n     \"The audit row at lines 184 to 186 already keeps the detail for people, so leave that code as it is.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_error_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"When a tool fails, the text sent to the model is a fixed message and never the server's error body.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_error_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R02\", LOOP,\n    \"Error text from tools reaches the model with no source or trust label, unlike results that succeed.\",\n    [\"Do R01 first. It replaces the error text with a fixed message, so no server text is left to label.\",\n     \"If you want the server's text kept, wrap it as `json.dumps({\\\"source\\\": spec.qualified, \\\"trust\\\": \\\"untrusted_data\\\", \\\"data\\\": ...})` like line 195.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_error_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"No text from a server reaches the model without the `untrusted_data` label or removal.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_error_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R03\", LOOP + [\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n    \"Error text reaches the model unredacted, and the approval text sent to the employee skips the link and image cleaner.\",\n    [\"Do R01 first. It fixes the error text at `src/agent.py` line 188.\",\n     \"In `src/main.py`, replace line 106 `body[\\\"approval\\\"] = state.pending_approval` with a copy whose `description` is cleaned.\",\n     \"The copy is `{**state.pending_approval, \\\"description\\\": sanitize_reply(state.pending_approval[\\\"description\\\"], CFG[\\\"output\\\"][\\\"allowed_link_hosts\\\"])}`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_approval_links.py`. Make it call `sanitize_reply` on a description with `![x](https://evil.example/a.png)` and assert `evil.example` is gone.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_approval_links.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"An approval text with an outside link or image shows no link or image to the employee.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"R04\", RET,\n    \"The search cache is keyed by query only, so one employee's private HR chunks can be returned to another.\",\n    [\"Do B02 first. It adds the employee id to the cache key in `src/retrieval.py`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_retrieval_cache.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"A second employee who repeats a query gets a fresh, filtered search and not the first employee's cached chunks.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_retrieval_cache.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R07\", LOOP + AUD,\n    \"Only the model-call audit row holds the context size. Tool rows and gateway rows drop it.\",\n    [\"Do not deploy the gateway change until the data-platform team has run step 2 on the database.\",\n     \"Create `migrations/002_context_tokens.sql` with `ALTER TABLE audit.gateway_decisions ADD COLUMN context_tokens integer;`. Ask the data-platform team to run it.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, after line 76, add `state.extra[\\\"context_tokens\\\"] = ctx_tokens`, indented 16 spaces.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, at lines 100, 103, 110, 115, 120, 174, 180, 184, 190 and 193, add `context_tokens=state.extra.get(\\\"context_tokens\\\")` to each `self.audit.record(` call.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway_client.py`, add the header `\\\"X-Context-Tokens\\\"` in `_post` and pass the value in. In `src/gateway.py` `_log`, store it in the new column.\",\n     \"Run a chat that uses a tool. In `audit.events`, check that the `tool_result` row has `context_tokens` set.\"],\n    \"Every tool action row in `audit.events` has `context_tokens` set, and so does its gateway row.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"R08\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No security detection rules or alert routing are in the repository. They may live in another system.\",\n    [\"Ask the security team for the rules that watch `run_stopped`, `tool_denied`, `approval_rejected`, `quota_denied` and `content_held` events.\",\n     \"Ask them to show who gets each alert and how fast.\",\n     \"Ask them to cause a test event of each kind in a test cluster and show that the alert arrived.\",\n     \"Save the rules and the test alert times in `docs/detection-evidence.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/detection-evidence.md` shows a test alert for each of the five event types reaching a named responder.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"R09\", [\"agent\", \"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n    \"Only fixed per-run limits exist. Nothing looks at chains of actions or adjusts limits for the size of the context.\",\n    [\"Ask the security team where chain rules can run, for example on the `audit.events` table. Ask who answers alerts.\",\n     \"Write down two chains to catch: a read of private data followed by `escalate_to_human`, and three denials in one run.\",\n     \"Create `docs/detection-rules.md` with the chains, the thresholds and the alert owner. Ask the security team to build the rules.\",\n     \"Ask them to replay a recorded run with each chain and show that the alert fires.\"],\n    \"`docs/detection-rules.md` lists the chains with thresholds, and a replayed run triggers each alert.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"R10\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No reviewer checks the agent's actions for misaligned behaviour, and no record says this risk is out of scope.\",\n    [\"Ask the business owner and the security lead to decide whether misaligned behaviour is in scope. Write the decision in `docs/misalignment-scope.md`.\",\n     \"If it is in scope, ask the model team to design a second reviewer that sees actions but not the untrusted text.\",\n     \"Ask them to build 20 labelled test traces, some evasive, and measure how many the reviewer misses.\",\n     \"Add the miss rate and the date to `docs/misalignment-scope.md`.\"],\n    \"`docs/misalignment-scope.md` holds a dated decision and, if in scope, the measured miss rate.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"R11\", DR,\n    \"The direct helpdesk route skips the gateway stop check, and the repository has no dated stop drill.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"In a test cluster, set a `fleet` flag in `control.stop_flags`. Check that a new chat and a tool call are both refused within 10 seconds. That limit is `max_stop_seconds` in `config/agent.yaml` line 51.\",\n     \"Repeat the drill with one flag each for `agent_instance`, `subject`, `agent_principal` and `agent_type`. Do the last one after B04.\",\n     \"Create `docs/stop-drill.md`. Write the date, who ran it, each scope tested, the seconds taken and the result.\",\n     \"Ask the operations lead to set a drill every three months and to review `docs/stop-drill.md`.\"],\n    \"`docs/stop-drill.md` shows a dated drill where every stop scope stopped the agent in 10 seconds.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"R12\", LOOP + [\"tool:file_leave_request\", \"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n    \"No stop rule says what happens to a leave request or ticket that was running when the agent stopped. Unknown outcomes are not held.\",\n    [\"Do R13 first. It records a row when a call is cancelled.\",\n     \"In `config/tools.yaml`, add `on_stop: complete_or_reconcile` to `file_leave_request` and `escalate_to_human`, and `on_stop: cancel` to the read tools.\",\n     \"In `src/tools.py`, add the field `on_stop: str = \\\"cancel\\\"` to `ToolSpec` and read it in `__init__` at line 47 with `on_stop=t.get(\\\"on_stop\\\", \\\"cancel\\\")`.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, in the `tool_outcome_unknown` handler from R13, write the `operation_id` into the audit row's `result`.\",\n     \"Ask the operations lead for a named owner who checks each `tool_outcome_unknown` row against HRIS and the helpdesk, and writes the result down.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_audit_steps.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"Every `tool_outcome_unknown` audit row has an operation id and a named owner who checks it.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_audit_steps.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R13\", LOOP,\n    \"The balance re-check call and cancelled tool calls leave no audit step. The direct retry also leaves none.\",\n    [\"Do B01 first. It removes the direct retry.\",\n     \"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_audit_steps.py` from the test below.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, after line 192 add `except asyncio.CancelledError:` at 12 spaces indent. Inside it add an `await self.audit.record(...)` for `\\\"tool_outcome_unknown\\\"` and then `raise`.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, replace lines 149 to 159 with a `_recheck_state` that takes `parent_step_id` and calls `self.audit.record` for `proposed_action` before and `tool_result` after the gateway call.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, change line 134 to call `self._recheck_state(ctx, state, spec, args, step_id)`.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, add `import asyncio` on the line before `import json` at line 4.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_audit_steps.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The balance re-check and a cancelled tool call each leave an audit row linked to the step.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_audit_steps.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R14\", [\"data:audit-log\", \"data:hr-postgres\", \"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n    \"Approval and audit rows are plain rows that anyone with write access could change. A gateway 503 also causes an automatic resend.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to export `audit.events` and `approvals.grants` every day to storage that cannot be changed, such as object lock.\",\n     \"In `src/approvals.py`, add a column `row_sha256` to the insert at line 46 that hashes `approval_id`, `operation`, `target`, `args_sha256` and `expires_at`.\",\n     \"In `pending()` at line 88, recompute that hash and raise `ApprovalInvalid` if it differs.\",\n     \"Create `migrations/003_grant_hash.sql` with `ALTER TABLE approvals.grants ADD COLUMN row_sha256 char(64);`. Ask the data-platform team to run it first.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_grant_hash.py` that changes a stored `args` value and checks `pending()` refuses it, then run it.\"],\n    \"A changed approval row is refused at resume, and daily exports of audit and approval rows exist.\",\n    \"large\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Agent\nadd(\"A01\", [\"agent\", \"api:sts\"],\n    \"The code gives the agent its own identity. Whether only that identity can be revoked is decided in systems outside this repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the identity team for the STS policy that issues tokens to `spiffe://acme.example/ns/hr-agent/sa/hr-helpdesk-agent`.\",\n     \"Ask them to revoke only that identity in a test cluster and show that employees' own logins still work.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to show that the database role `hr_agent` can be locked without touching `hr_gateway`.\",\n     \"Save the policy and the drill results in `docs/identity-evidence.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/identity-evidence.md` shows a dated drill that revoked only the agent identity.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"A02\", [\"agent\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\", \"data:audit-log\"],\n    \"Requests that fail sign-in are not audited at the agent. In the gateway they are logged with `unknown` identity fields.\",\n    [\"In `src/main.py`, in `chat` at line 113 and in `confirm` at line 139, add a `log.warning(\\\"unauthenticated request\\\", extra={\\\"path\\\": str(request.url.path)})` before each 401.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to add table `audit.preauth_denials` with `ts`, `path`, `peer` and `reason`. Then write one row there at both places.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, change `_log` so that a failed write raises instead of being skipped at line 196, and return 503.\",\n     \"Create `docs/audit-fields.md` listing which of the six fields each pre-sign-in row can fill, and why the others are `unknown`.\",\n     \"Send a bad token to `/v1/chat` in a test cluster. Check that one row appears in `audit.preauth_denials`.\"],\n    \"A request with a bad token leaves one audit row, and a failed audit write makes the gateway answer 503.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"A03\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"`.mcp.json` is not part of the type ID, so changing it does not change the agent's identity.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_type_id.py` from the test below.\",\n     \"In `src/type_id.py`, change line 21 to `INPUT_FILES = (\\\"requirements.txt\\\", \\\"Dockerfile\\\", \\\".mcp.json\\\")`.\",\n     \"In `Dockerfile`, change line 12 to `COPY --chown=0:0 requirements.txt Dockerfile .mcp.json ./`. The file must be in the image, or the pod stops at start.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_type_id.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"Make the same change to `README.md` line 60, which lists the inputs.\"],\n    \"Changing `.mcp.json` changes the agent type ID, and the same files give the same ID twice.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_type_id.py\"))\n\nadd(\"A04\", GW + [\"agent\"],\n    \"The gateway trusts an instance ID and a trace ID that the caller writes in a header. A resumed approval also starts a new trace.\",\n    [\"Ask the identity team to add the claim `agent_instance_id` to tokens. Do not deploy the next steps until they have shipped it.\",\n     \"In `src/credentials.py`, add `ctx` data to `token()` so the claim is requested, and add the instance to the cache key at line 42.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, at line 170, read `instance = claims[\\\"agent_instance_id\\\"]` instead of the header.\",\n     \"In `migrations/001_init.sql` line 54, add the column `traceparent text` to `approvals.grants`. Store it in `request()` and restore it in `resume_with_approval`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_gateway_instance.py`. Send a call with a header that differs from the claim, and assert the claim is used.\",\n     \"Run the new test with `python -m pytest tests/test_gateway_instance.py`.\"],\n    \"The gateway uses the instance ID from the signed token. A header value cannot change which flag or rate limit applies.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"A05\", GW + AUD,\n    \"A stop flag for one agent type is not enforced at the gateway. Gateway audit rows keep IDs that the caller supplied.\",\n    [\"Do B04 first. It adds the `agent_type` stop scope and a signed `agent_type_id`.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, in `_log` at lines 137 to 139, replace the two `request.headers.get(...)` values with `c.get(\\\"agent_type_id\\\")` and the verified instance.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to rename the columns at `migrations/001_init.sql` line 23 to `agent_type_id` and `agent_instance_id`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_gateway_stop.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"In a test cluster, call the gateway with a spoofed header. Check the audit row holds the token's value.\"],\n    \"A flag with scope `agent_type` stops calls at the gateway, and its audit rows hold the signed type ID.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_gateway_stop.py\"))\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Configuration\nadd(\"C01\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The release manifest leaves out the issuers, audiences, MCP versions, tool fingerprints and cache settings. Most entries have no owner.\",\n    [\"In `release/manifest.yaml`, add to `identity_bindings` after line 71 the keys `sso: {issuer: https://sso.acme.example, audience: hr-helpdesk}` and `sts: {issuer: https://sts.acme.example, audience: hr-tool-gateway}`.\",\n     \"Add a key `mcp_protocol` under `tools` with the version the gateway speaks. Ask the gateway owner for it.\",\n     \"Under each server at lines 54 and 55, add `fingerprints: config/tools.yaml` and a `settings` key naming the retrieval cache ttl `cache_ttl_seconds: 900`.\",\n     \"For `system_prompt`, `configuration`, `network` and `admission`, add an `owner` and a `ref` with the git commit or file digest.\",\n     \"Run `python -c \\\"import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('release/manifest.yaml'))\\\"` to check the file still loads.\"],\n    \"`release/manifest.yaml` has issuer and audience for both token services and an owner for every entry.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"C02\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"One catch-all code owner can change the Dockerfile, dependencies and most of `src/` alone. No emergency change path is written down.\",\n    [\"In `CODEOWNERS`, insert three lines after line 1: `/src/`, `/Dockerfile` and `/requirements.txt`. Give each `@acme/people-platform @acme/security-engineering`.\",\n     \"Keep line 4 (`/src/gateway.py`) and line 5 below them, because the last matching line wins.\",\n     \"Create `docs/emergency-change.md`. Write who may approve an urgent change, how it is recorded, and when review happens after it.\",\n     \"Ask the repository admin to confirm that code-owner review is required on `main`.\",\n     \"Open a test pull request that changes `Dockerfile`. Check that GitHub asks for `@acme/security-engineering`.\"],\n    \"A pull request that changes `Dockerfile`, `requirements.txt` or `src/` needs the security team to review it.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"C03\", [\"agent\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n    \"Only the agent checks its own identity at start. Nothing outside it compares the running prompt, model and tools to the approved manifest.\",\n    [\"Create `k8s/identity-check.yaml` with a CronJob that runs every 15 minutes in `hr-agent`. Ask the platform team which image it should use.\",\n     \"Make the job read the `AGENT_TYPE_ID` of each running pod, and compare it to `agent_type_id` in the stored manifest for that release.\",\n     \"Make the job send an alert to the security channel and set a stop flag of scope `agent_type` when they differ.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to run the job against a test pod with a changed prompt. Check that the alert fires.\"],\n    \"A pod whose type ID differs from the approved manifest causes an alert within 15 minutes.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"C04\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No check compares the running prompts, tools, permissions and network rules with the approved baseline.\",\n    [\"Do C03 first. It adds the scheduled job.\",\n     \"Extend that job to hash the live `NetworkPolicy`, the `ClusterPolicy` and `tools.yaml` and compare them to hashes in `release/manifest.yaml`.\",\n     \"In `config/agent.yaml`, add a `drift` block with `alert_channel`, `response: stop_agent_type` and `max_minutes: 15`.\",\n     \"Change one network rule in a test cluster. Check that the alert and the response happen within 15 minutes.\"],\n    \"A changed network rule or tool file in a test cluster triggers an alert and a stop within 15 minutes.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"C05\", [\"model:claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\"],\n    \"Nothing re-tests the hosted model on a schedule or watches for provider notices.\",\n    [\"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, add a new workflow `.github/workflows/model-retest.yml` with `on: schedule` set to weekly.\",\n     \"Make the new workflow run `python -m pytest -q tests/release`, the same tests as the release.\",\n     \"Ask the model team to subscribe to the Anthropic model deprecation notices and name an owner in `release/manifest.yaml` under `models.primary`.\",\n     \"Trigger the workflow by hand once and check that it runs the tests.\"],\n    \"A weekly job runs the release tests against the pinned model, and a named person watches provider notices.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"C06\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The release job runs tests in `tests/release`, but that folder does not exist. Results are not saved with the release.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests/release`. Create `tests/release/test_approval_text.py` from the test below, as a first case.\",\n     \"Add one test file for each of: denied destructive action, access limits, prompt injection, audit rows, stopping, retrieval and checkers.\",\n     \"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, change line 58 to a list of lines naming `type-id.json`, `release/manifest.yaml` and `test-results.xml`.\",\n     \"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, change line 29 to `python -m pytest -q tests/release --junitxml=test-results.xml`.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to add a job after `build` that runs the same tests inside the built image digest.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/release`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The release job runs real tests and uploads `test-results.xml` with the manifest.\",\n    \"large\", {\"file\": \"tests/release/test_approval_text.py\", \"code\": (TRIAL / \"tests/test_approval_text.py\").read_text(),\n              \"run\": PYTEST + \"tests/release/test_approval_text.py\"})\n\nadd(\"C07\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"There is no stored earlier release, rollback steps or model retirement date.\",\n    [\"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, add a `rollback` job after line 75 that takes an old `git_sha` and re-applies its stored manifest.\",\n     \"Keep each release's manifest by digest. Ask the platform team where to store them.\",\n     \"In `release/manifest.yaml` under `models.primary`, add `retirement_date` from the provider notice. Ask the model team for it.\",\n     \"Create `docs/rollback.md` saying how to drain pending approvals and discard the cached index on rollback.\",\n     \"Run the rollback job once in a test cluster. Check that the older version answers a chat.\"],\n    \"A tested rollback job exists and the manifest holds the model retirement date.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"C08\", GW + AUD,\n    \"Gateway rows cannot be tied to a stored release manifest, and audit rows are kept about six weeks instead of six months.\",\n    [\"Do E11 first. It fixes how long audit rows are kept.\",\n     \"Do A05 first. It stores a signed type ID in gateway rows.\",\n     \"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, upload the manifest under the name `manifest-<agent_type_id>` so it can be found by type ID.\",\n     \"In a test cluster, take one gateway row. Find its manifest using the stored type ID.\"],\n    \"From any gateway audit row you can find the exact release manifest by its type ID.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Ecosystem\nadd(\"E01\", [\"agent\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\", \"api:sts\"],\n    \"No inventory covers the gateway, token service, registry, audit store and stop service. Entries have only one owner.\",\n    [\"In `release/manifest.yaml`, add a `services` list after line 55.\",\n     \"Add an entry for the gateway, STS, JWKS, image registry, Postgres and the telemetry collector.\",\n     \"Give each entry `agent_team_owner` and `provider_owner`.\",\n     \"Run `python -c \\\"import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('release/manifest.yaml'))\\\"` to check the file loads.\"],\n    \"Every outside service the agent uses has two named owners in `release/manifest.yaml`.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"E02\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No scan for known weaknesses runs in CI, and there are no records about who publishes each dependency.\",\n    [\"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, add a step after line 28: `- run: pip install pip-audit && pip-audit -r requirements.txt --require-hashes`.\",\n     \"Create `docs/dependencies.md`. For each line in `requirements.txt`, write publisher, permissions and update source.\",\n     \"For `hris` and `helpdesk` in `config/tools.yaml`, add the publisher and update source next to `owner`.\",\n     \"Push a test branch. Check that the new step runs and the job fails when a known bad version is listed.\"],\n    \"The release job fails when a dependency has a known weakness, and every dependency has a record.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"E03\", DR,\n    \"Tool fingerprints are checked only every 300 seconds, a list change message is ignored, and a gateway error skips the check.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, call `refresh_fingerprints()` before the tool lookup at line 165, with a short time limit. Refuse the call if it fails.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py` line 213, lower the sleep from 300 to 60 seconds.\",\n     \"In `config/tools.yaml`, add `implementation_ref` with the server's image digest under `hris` and `helpdesk`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_fingerprint.py` that changes a live description and asserts the tool is disabled. Run it.\"],\n    \"A changed tool description disables the tool before the next call and not after five minutes.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E04\", GW + [\"tool:search_policies\"],\n    \"Server instructions, descriptions and schemas are only fingerprinted. They are never scanned for hidden instructions.\",\n    [\"In `src/gateway.py`, add `scan_metadata(tool)` that rejects zero-width and control characters, long strings and phrases like `ignore previous`.\",\n     \"Call it from `refresh_fingerprints` at line 64 for every live tool, and disable the tool when it fails.\",\n     \"Also fetch `initialize` server `instructions` and scan them the same way.\",\n     \"Add a unit test with a description holding a zero-width character. Assert the tool is disabled.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_metadata_scan.py`.\"],\n    \"A tool with hidden characters or override words in its metadata is disabled before the model sees it.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E05\", GW,\n    \"Lookalike tool names across servers are only logged. Tricks such as Cyrillic letters are not detected.\",\n    [\"In `src/gateway.py`, replace the `log.error` at line 67 with `_disabled.update(...)` for every tool in the clash.\",\n     \"At line 65, add a confusables map for Cyrillic and Greek letters before the `casefold()` call.\",\n     \"In `src/approvals.py`, add the server id to the approval text in `describe()`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_lookalike.py` with the names `create_ticket` and `create_tіcket` (Cyrillic i). Assert both are disabled. Run it.\"],\n    \"Two tools whose names look alike are both disabled and the clash is logged.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E06\", DR,\n    \"When the gateway returns 503 the client sends `escalate_to_human` straight to the helpdesk server and skips the gateway.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Check `.mcp.json` and `src/gateway_client.py` for any other URL that is not `GATEWAY_URL`. There should be none.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_direct_route.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The only network route to the helpdesk server goes through the gateway.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_direct_route.py\"))\n\nadd(\"E09\", DR + [\"api:sts\"],\n    \"A stop flag does not revoke tokens already issued. They last 300 seconds, and the direct route skips the stop check.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"In `src/credentials.py`, change line 20 from `300` to `60` so a stop is effective sooner.\",\n     \"In `src/credentials.py`, call `drop_subject` from `StopControl` when it cancels a run (`src/killswitch.py` line 58).\",\n     \"Ask the identity team for a revoke call. Call it for the subject when a stop flag appears.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, record in-flight tool calls at stop. R13 adds this record.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_audit_steps.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"After a stop, a copied token is refused within 60 seconds and every in-flight call has an audit row.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_audit_steps.py\"))\n\nadd(\"E10\", GW + DR,\n    \"Gateway audit rows lack verified identity and the vendor's receipt ID, and an allow row is written only after the action.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Do A05 first. It stores a signed type ID in gateway rows.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, at line 190, add the `request_id` or `ticket_id` from `structured` to the reason written by `_log`.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, write a `pending` row before line 177 and update it after line 190. Return 503 if the first write fails.\",\n     \"Run a ticket call in a test cluster. Check the `audit.gateway_decisions` row holds the ticket id.\"],\n    \"Every gateway call has a row written before it runs and holds the vendor receipt ID after.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E11\", AUD,\n    \"Audit rows are kept about six weeks, not six months. Nothing shows if rows are missing or changed.\",\n    [\"In `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`, change line 35 from `\\\"6\\\"` to `\\\"27\\\"`. That is 26 weeks plus a spare.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to add a `seq bigserial` column to `audit.events` and alert on gaps in it.\",\n     \"Ask them to export audit rows each day to storage that cannot be changed, and to alert if the export fails.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, write the audit row before forwarding the call. E10 covers this.\",\n     \"After the next night's run, ask the data-platform team to check that the oldest partition is about 26 weeks old.\"],\n    \"The oldest `audit.events` partition is at least 26 weeks old, and a gap in `seq` causes an alert.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E12\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No runbook, alert route, fleet impact query or outside-reporting owner is in the repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the security lead to write the runbook for an incident that affects every agent of this type, and create `docs/incident-runbook.md`.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team for a query that lists all runs and subjects touched by one agent type ID in a time range.\",\n     \"Name the person who decides on outside reporting in the runbook.\",\n     \"Run a drill: stop, quarantine and revoke the agent in a test cluster. Record the alert times in the runbook.\",\n     \"Check that `docs/incident-runbook.md` has the query, the owner, the alert times and the drill date.\"],\n    \"`docs/incident-runbook.md` holds a fleet impact query, a named reporting owner and a dated drill result.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\npath = AGENT / \"brace-findings.json\"\ndata = json.loads(path.read_text())\ncount = 0\nfor f in data[\"findings\"]:\n    if f[\"rating\"] in (\"gap\", \"needs_evidence\"):\n        entry = F.pop(f[\"item\"])\n        f[\"components\"] = entry[\"components\"]\n        f[\"fix\"] = entry[\"fix\"]\n        f[\"assignee\"] = None\n        count += 1\nassert not F, f\"unused fixes: {list(F)}\"\npath.write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\nprint(\"updated\", count)\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RJmSYwKawMBKQ87TEiaZig","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-action-_pgwuimk/scratch/make_fixes.py (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"981bf4ba-51f4-44d7-811c-79f7b4ddcca3","uuid":"882788a0-53d4-41d6-92d4-2e0da174111c","timestamp":"2026-11-21T12:39:49.797Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-action-_pgwuimk/scratch/make_fixes.py","content":"\"\"\"Adds components, fix and assignee to gap / needs_evidence findings. Touches nothing else.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport sys\n\nAGENT = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])\nTRIAL = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[2])\nPYTEST = \"python -m pytest \"\n\n\ndef test_of(name):\n    return {\"file\": f\"tests/{name}\", \"code\": (TRIAL / \"tests\" / name).read_text(), \"run\": PYTEST + f\"tests/{name}\"}\n\n\nDR = [\"tool:escalate_to_human\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\", \"mcp:helpdesk\"]\nGW = [\"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"]\nRET = [\"tool:search_policies\", \"data:hr-postgres\"]\nAPPR = [\"tool:file_leave_request\", \"tool:escalate_to_human\"]\nAUD = [\"data:audit-log\"]\nLOOP = [\"unit:src/agent.py\"]\nALL = [\"agent\"]\n\nF = {}\n\n\ndef add(item, comps, problem, steps, done, effort, test=None):\n    F[item] = {\"components\": comps, \"fix\": {\"problem\": problem, \"steps\": steps, \"done_when\": done, \"effort\": effort}}\n    if test:\n        F[item][\"fix\"][\"test\"] = test\n\n\nDO_B01 = \"Do B01 first. It removes the direct route to the helpdesk server.\"\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Build time\nadd(\"B01\", DR,\n    \"If the gateway returns 503, `escalate_to_human` sends the call straight to the helpdesk server. That skips the gateway allowlist and stop checks.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests`. Create the file `tests/test_direct_route.py` from the test below. It fails until the next steps are done.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway_client.py`, replace lines 46 to 59 (the `try` and the whole `except GatewayUnavailable` block) with the two statements shown after this list, indented 8 spaces.\",\n     \"The first statement is `token = await self._creds.token(audience=GATEWAY_AUDIENCE, scope=spec.scope, subject_token=subject_token, subject=ctx.subject)`.\",\n     \"The second statement is `return await self._post(GATEWAY_URL, token, spec, args, ctx, operation_id)`.\",\n     \"In `config/tools.yaml`, delete lines 91 to 93. These are the `direct_route:` key and its `endpoint` and `audience` lines.\",\n     \"In `k8s/networkpolicy.yaml`, delete lines 48 to 50. This is the rule that lets the agent reach `helpdesk-mcp`. Keep the gateway rule at lines 76 to 79.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_direct_route.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"When the gateway returns 503, `escalate_to_human` fails and no request goes to the helpdesk server.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_direct_route.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B02\", RET + [\"agent\"],\n    \"The handbook search cache is keyed by query text only. One employee can be served another employee's private handbook chunks.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_retrieval_cache.py` from the test below. It fails until the next steps are done.\",\n     \"In `src/retrieval.py`, change line 46 to `key = self._key(query, employee_id)`. Do this before the next step, because it is lower in the file.\",\n     \"In `src/retrieval.py`, replace lines 40 to 42 with a `_key(self, query: str, employee_id: str)` method that keeps the `normalized` line.\",\n     \"Make that method end with `return hashlib.sha256(f\\\"{self._top_k}|{employee_id}|{normalized}\\\".encode()).hexdigest()`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_retrieval_cache.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"Ask the identity team to send you the STS scope policy and the HRIS and helpdesk audience rules, and keep them with the review record.\"],\n    \"Two employees who search the same words each get their own results, never the other's cached chunks.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_retrieval_cache.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B03\", [\"agent\", \"data:hr-postgres\"],\n    \"The database passwords and the Anthropic key are fixed secrets in `k8s/deployment.yaml`. No rotation or expiry is shown in the repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the platform team for the rotation schedule of the secrets `hr-agent-db`, `hr-gateway-db` and `hr-agent-anthropic`. Ask who owns each.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team whether the database accepts short-lived logins instead of a fixed password. Ask for the answer in writing.\",\n     \"Ask the identity team to confirm that tokens for the helpdesk and HRIS servers carry a `cnf` certificate binding.\",\n     \"Save the answers in `docs/credential-evidence.md`, and create that file. Give each secret an owner, a rotation date and a next review date.\",\n     \"Check that every secret named in `k8s/deployment.yaml` appears in that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/credential-evidence.md` lists every secret with an owner, a rotation period and the last rotation date.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"B04\", DR,\n    \"A stop flag does not reach every path. The direct helpdesk route skips the gateway stop check, and the gateway ignores `agent_type` flags.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Ask the identity team to add a signed claim named `agent_type_id` to the tokens that the gateway accepts. Do not deploy step 3 until they have shipped it.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, change line 84 so the `require` list also contains `\\\"agent_type_id\\\"`. Do this after step 4, because it is higher in the file.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, replace lines 101 and 102 so the query also has `OR (scope = 'agent_type' AND value = $4)` and the arguments end with `claims[\\\"agent_type_id\\\"]`.\",\n     \"Create the test below as `tests/test_gateway_stop.py`. Run `python -m pytest tests/test_gateway_stop.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"Write in `README.md` under \\\"Stopping the agent\\\" that tokens last up to 300 seconds and a stop flag is checked on every call.\"],\n    \"A stop flag with scope `agent_type` makes the gateway refuse that agent type's calls.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_gateway_stop.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B05\", APPR,\n    \"The approval text for a leave request leaves out the `note` the model wrote. The employee approves arguments they were never shown.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_approval_text.py` from the test below. One test fails until the next step is done.\",\n     \"In `src/approvals.py`, replace lines 30 to 32 so the leave text is stored in a variable named `text`.\",\n     \"After that, add `if args.get(\\\"note\\\"):` and, inside it, `text += f\\\" Your note to the manager: \\\\\\\"{args['note']}\\\\\\\"\\\"`. Then add `return text`. Keep all of it inside the first `if`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_approval_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The approval text for a leave request shows the note that will be sent.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_approval_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B06\", APPR,\n    \"The reviewer sees the leave type and dates but not the `note`, even though the approval hash covers the note.\",\n    [\"Do B05 first. It adds the note to `describe()` in `src/approvals.py`.\",\n     \"Open `describe()` in `src/approvals.py`. Check that every key in `input_schema` for each tool in `config/tools.yaml` appears in its text.\",\n     \"If you add a field to a tool later, add it to `describe()` in the same change.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_approval_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The text an employee approves contains every argument that is sent, including the note.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_approval_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"B07\", [\"agent\", \"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n    \"The Anthropic client retries once on its own and only the last answer is counted. Concurrent runs can also pass the quota before it is recorded.\",\n    [\"In `src/main.py`, change line 172 from `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=1)` to `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=0)`. A failed call now fails once and is counted.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_budget_concurrency.py`. Make it start 30 calls to `QuotaStore.reserve_run` at once against a test database with a limit of 20 runs.\",\n     \"In that test, assert that exactly 20 calls succeed and 10 raise `BudgetExceeded`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_budget_concurrency.py`. Ask the platform team to run it against a real Postgres, because the repository has no test database.\"],\n    \"No more runs start than the quota allows, and a failed model call is not retried out of sight.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"B08\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The network and runtime files look correct, but nothing shows that they work in a running cluster.\",\n    [\"Ask the platform team to run a pod with the agent's labels in `hr-agent` and try to reach a public site. It should fail.\",\n     \"Ask them to try `169.254.169.254` from the same pod. It should fail too.\",\n     \"Ask them to try `hris-mcp` directly from the agent pod. It should fail, since only the gateway may reach it.\",\n     \"Save the commands, the dates and the results in `docs/egress-test.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/egress-test.md` shows a dated test where a public site, the metadata address and `hris-mcp` were all refused.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"B09\", DR,\n    \"The agent pod can reach the helpdesk server directly, and the client uses that path when the gateway is down.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Check that `k8s/networkpolicy.yaml` no longer has the `helpdesk-mcp` rule in the `hr-helpdesk-agent-egress` policy.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to try a call from the agent pod to `helpdesk-mcp` on port 8443. It must be refused.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_direct_route.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The agent pod cannot open a connection to `helpdesk-mcp`; only the gateway can.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"B10\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"Admission does not deny images that match no signing rule. The `platform/*` rule also checks no build attestation.\",\n    [\"In `k8s/admission.yaml`, add a rule after line 81 named `deny-unverified-images`, indented 4 spaces like the other rules.\",\n     \"Make that rule match Pods in `hr-agent` and use a `validate` block with a `deny` condition for any image that does not start with `registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent` or `registry.acme.example/platform/`.\",\n     \"Under the `platform/*` entry at line 72, add an `attestations` block like lines 51 to 71. Ask the platform team which build file to name.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to try a test pod with `registry.acme.example/other/app@sha256:...` in `hr-agent`. It must be refused.\"],\n    \"A pod in `hr-agent` with an image outside the two approved paths is refused by admission.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"B11\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The audit CronJob uses the `platform/psql` image. Its contents cannot be seen in this repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the platform team for the file list or SBOM of `registry.acme.example/platform/psql` at the digest in `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml` line 26.\",\n     \"Check the list for a shell, `curl`, `wget` and a package manager.\",\n     \"If any is present, ask the platform team to build a smaller image and put its new digest on line 26.\",\n     \"Save the SBOM and your check in `docs/psql-image-check.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/psql-image-check.md` shows the image has no shell, downloader or package manager.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"B12\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"Review rules for the `main` branch are repository settings. They are not in the code, so force-push and delete rules cannot be seen.\",\n    [\"Ask the repository admin to export the ruleset for `main` from the GitHub settings page.\",\n     \"Check that it blocks force-pushes and deletion and that it requires review by the code owners in `CODEOWNERS`.\",\n     \"Check that only the `release.yml` workflow can deploy, and that nobody can start it by hand.\",\n     \"Save the export in `docs/branch-protection.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/branch-protection.md` shows force-push and delete are blocked on `main` and code-owner review is required.\",\n    \"small\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Run time\nERR_STEP = (\"In `src/agent.py`, find the line `return _tool_result(tool_use_id, f\\\"{spec.name} failed: {exc.detail}\\\", error=True)` (line 188). \"\n            \"Change the text to `f\\\"{spec.name} failed. The details were recorded for review.\\\"`.\")\n\nadd(\"R01\", LOOP,\n    \"Error text from tools and the gateway goes to the model without any check on its size, content or safety.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_error_text.py` from the test below.\",\n     ERR_STEP,\n     \"The audit row at lines 184 to 186 already keeps the detail for people, so leave that code as it is.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_error_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"When a tool fails, the text sent to the model is a fixed message and never the server's error body.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_error_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R02\", LOOP,\n    \"Error text from tools reaches the model with no source or trust label, unlike results that succeed.\",\n    [\"Do R01 first. It replaces the error text with a fixed message, so no server text is left to label.\",\n     \"If you want the server's text kept, wrap it as `json.dumps({\\\"source\\\": spec.qualified, \\\"trust\\\": \\\"untrusted_data\\\", \\\"data\\\": ...})` like line 195.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_error_text.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"No text from a server reaches the model without the `untrusted_data` label or removal.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_error_text.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R03\", LOOP + [\"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n    \"Error text reaches the model unredacted, and the approval text sent to the employee skips the link and image cleaner.\",\n    [\"Do R01 first. It fixes the error text at `src/agent.py` line 188.\",\n     \"In `src/main.py`, replace line 106 `body[\\\"approval\\\"] = state.pending_approval` with a copy whose `description` is cleaned.\",\n     \"The copy is `{**state.pending_approval, \\\"description\\\": sanitize_reply(state.pending_approval[\\\"description\\\"], CFG[\\\"output\\\"][\\\"allowed_link_hosts\\\"])}`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_approval_links.py`. Make it call `sanitize_reply` on a description with `![x](https://evil.example/a.png)` and assert `evil.example` is gone.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_approval_links.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"An approval text with an outside link or image shows no link or image to the employee.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"R04\", RET,\n    \"The search cache is keyed by query only, so one employee's private HR chunks can be returned to another.\",\n    [\"Do B02 first. It adds the employee id to the cache key in `src/retrieval.py`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_retrieval_cache.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"A second employee who repeats a query gets a fresh, filtered search and not the first employee's cached chunks.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_retrieval_cache.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R07\", LOOP + AUD,\n    \"Only the model-call audit row holds the context size. Tool rows and gateway rows drop it.\",\n    [\"Do not deploy the gateway change until the data-platform team has run step 2 on the database.\",\n     \"Create `migrations/002_context_tokens.sql` with `ALTER TABLE audit.gateway_decisions ADD COLUMN context_tokens integer;`. Ask the data-platform team to run it.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, after line 76, add `state.extra[\\\"context_tokens\\\"] = ctx_tokens`, indented 16 spaces.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, at lines 100, 103, 110, 115, 120, 174, 180, 184, 190 and 193, add `context_tokens=state.extra.get(\\\"context_tokens\\\")` to each `self.audit.record(` call.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway_client.py`, add the header `\\\"X-Context-Tokens\\\"` in `_post` and pass the value in. In `src/gateway.py` `_log`, store it in the new column.\",\n     \"Run a chat that uses a tool. In `audit.events`, check that the `tool_result` row has `context_tokens` set.\"],\n    \"Every tool action row in `audit.events` has `context_tokens` set, and so does its gateway row.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"R08\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No security detection rules or alert routing are in the repository. They may live in another system.\",\n    [\"Ask the security team for the rules that watch `run_stopped`, `tool_denied`, `approval_rejected`, `quota_denied` and `content_held` events.\",\n     \"Ask them to show who gets each alert and how fast.\",\n     \"Ask them to cause a test event of each kind in a test cluster and show that the alert arrived.\",\n     \"Save the rules and the test alert times in `docs/detection-evidence.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/detection-evidence.md` shows a test alert for each of the five event types reaching a named responder.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"R09\", [\"agent\", \"unit:src/agent.py\"],\n    \"Only fixed per-run limits exist. Nothing looks at chains of actions or adjusts limits for the size of the context.\",\n    [\"Ask the security team where chain rules can run, for example on the `audit.events` table. Ask who answers alerts.\",\n     \"Write down two chains to catch: a read of private data followed by `escalate_to_human`, and three denials in one run.\",\n     \"Create `docs/detection-rules.md` with the chains, the thresholds and the alert owner. Ask the security team to build the rules.\",\n     \"Ask them to replay a recorded run with each chain and show that the alert fires.\"],\n    \"`docs/detection-rules.md` lists the chains with thresholds, and a replayed run triggers each alert.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"R10\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No reviewer checks the agent's actions for misaligned behaviour, and no record says this risk is out of scope.\",\n    [\"Ask the business owner and the security lead to decide whether misaligned behaviour is in scope. Write the decision in `docs/misalignment-scope.md`.\",\n     \"If it is in scope, ask the model team to design a second reviewer that sees actions but not the untrusted text.\",\n     \"Ask them to build 20 labelled test traces, some evasive, and measure how many the reviewer misses.\",\n     \"Add the miss rate and the date to `docs/misalignment-scope.md`.\"],\n    \"`docs/misalignment-scope.md` holds a dated decision and, if in scope, the measured miss rate.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"R11\", DR,\n    \"The direct helpdesk route skips the gateway stop check, and the repository has no dated stop drill.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"In a test cluster, set a `fleet` flag in `control.stop_flags`. Check that a new chat and a tool call are both refused within 10 seconds. That limit is `max_stop_seconds` in `config/agent.yaml` line 51.\",\n     \"Repeat the drill with one flag each for `agent_instance`, `subject`, `agent_principal` and `agent_type`. Do the last one after B04.\",\n     \"Create `docs/stop-drill.md`. Write the date, who ran it, each scope tested, the seconds taken and the result.\",\n     \"Ask the operations lead to set a drill every three months and to review `docs/stop-drill.md`.\"],\n    \"`docs/stop-drill.md` shows a dated drill where every stop scope stopped the agent in 10 seconds.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"R12\", LOOP + [\"tool:file_leave_request\", \"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n    \"No stop rule says what happens to a leave request or ticket that was running when the agent stopped. Unknown outcomes are not held.\",\n    [\"Do R13 first. It records a row when a call is cancelled.\",\n     \"In `config/tools.yaml`, add `on_stop: complete_or_reconcile` to `file_leave_request` and `escalate_to_human`, and `on_stop: cancel` to the read tools.\",\n     \"In `src/tools.py`, add the field `on_stop: str = \\\"cancel\\\"` to `ToolSpec` and read it in `__init__` at line 47 with `on_stop=t.get(\\\"on_stop\\\", \\\"cancel\\\")`.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, in the `tool_outcome_unknown` handler from R13, write the `operation_id` into the audit row's `result`.\",\n     \"Ask the operations lead for a named owner who checks each `tool_outcome_unknown` row against HRIS and the helpdesk, and writes the result down.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_audit_steps.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"Every `tool_outcome_unknown` audit row has an operation id and a named owner who checks it.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_audit_steps.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R13\", LOOP,\n    \"The balance re-check call and cancelled tool calls leave no audit step. The direct retry also leaves none.\",\n    [\"Do B01 first. It removes the direct retry.\",\n     \"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_audit_steps.py` from the test below.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, after line 192 add `except asyncio.CancelledError:` at 12 spaces indent. Inside it add an `await self.audit.record(...)` for `\\\"tool_outcome_unknown\\\"` and then `raise`.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, replace lines 149 to 159 with a `_recheck_state` that takes `parent_step_id` and calls `self.audit.record` for `proposed_action` before and `tool_result` after the gateway call.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, change line 134 to call `self._recheck_state(ctx, state, spec, args, step_id)`.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, add `import asyncio` on the line before `import json` at line 4.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_audit_steps.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The balance re-check and a cancelled tool call each leave an audit row linked to the step.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_audit_steps.py\"))\n\nadd(\"R14\", [\"data:audit-log\", \"data:hr-postgres\", \"tool:escalate_to_human\"],\n    \"Approval and audit rows are plain rows that anyone with write access could change. A gateway 503 also causes an automatic resend.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to export `audit.events` and `approvals.grants` every day to storage that cannot be changed, such as object lock.\",\n     \"In `src/approvals.py`, add a column `row_sha256` to the insert at line 46 that hashes `approval_id`, `operation`, `target`, `args_sha256` and `expires_at`.\",\n     \"In `pending()` at line 88, recompute that hash and raise `ApprovalInvalid` if it differs.\",\n     \"Create `migrations/003_grant_hash.sql` with `ALTER TABLE approvals.grants ADD COLUMN row_sha256 char(64);`. Ask the data-platform team to run it first.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_grant_hash.py` that changes a stored `args` value and checks `pending()` refuses it, then run it.\"],\n    \"A changed approval row is refused at resume, and daily exports of audit and approval rows exist.\",\n    \"large\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Agent\nadd(\"A01\", [\"agent\", \"api:sts\"],\n    \"The code gives the agent its own identity. Whether only that identity can be revoked is decided in systems outside this repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the identity team for the STS policy that issues tokens to `spiffe://acme.example/ns/hr-agent/sa/hr-helpdesk-agent`.\",\n     \"Ask them to revoke only that identity in a test cluster and show that employees' own logins still work.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to show that the database role `hr_agent` can be locked without touching `hr_gateway`.\",\n     \"Save the policy and the drill results in `docs/identity-evidence.md`, and create that file.\"],\n    \"`docs/identity-evidence.md` shows a dated drill that revoked only the agent identity.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"A02\", [\"agent\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\", \"data:audit-log\"],\n    \"Requests that fail sign-in are not audited at the agent. In the gateway they are logged with `unknown` identity fields.\",\n    [\"In `src/main.py`, in `chat` at line 113 and in `confirm` at line 139, add a `log.warning(\\\"unauthenticated request\\\", extra={\\\"path\\\": str(request.url.path)})` before each 401.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to add table `audit.preauth_denials` with `ts`, `path`, `peer` and `reason`. Then write one row there at both places.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, change `_log` so that a failed write raises instead of being skipped at line 196, and return 503.\",\n     \"Create `docs/audit-fields.md` listing which of the six fields each pre-sign-in row can fill, and why the others are `unknown`.\",\n     \"Send a bad token to `/v1/chat` in a test cluster. Check that one row appears in `audit.preauth_denials`.\"],\n    \"A request with a bad token leaves one audit row, and a failed audit write makes the gateway answer 503.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"A03\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"`.mcp.json` is not part of the type ID, so changing it does not change the agent's identity.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests` if it is missing. Create `tests/test_type_id.py` from the test below.\",\n     \"In `src/type_id.py`, change line 21 to `INPUT_FILES = (\\\"requirements.txt\\\", \\\"Dockerfile\\\", \\\".mcp.json\\\")`.\",\n     \"In `Dockerfile`, change line 12 to `COPY --chown=0:0 requirements.txt Dockerfile .mcp.json ./`. The file must be in the image, or the pod stops at start.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_type_id.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"Make the same change to `README.md` line 60, which lists the inputs.\"],\n    \"Changing `.mcp.json` changes the agent type ID, and the same files give the same ID twice.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_type_id.py\"))\n\nadd(\"A04\", GW + [\"agent\"],\n    \"The gateway trusts an instance ID and a trace ID that the caller writes in a header. A resumed approval also starts a new trace.\",\n    [\"Ask the identity team to add the claim `agent_instance_id` to tokens. Do not deploy the next steps until they have shipped it.\",\n     \"In `src/credentials.py`, add `ctx` data to `token()` so the claim is requested, and add the instance to the cache key at line 42.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, at line 170, read `instance = claims[\\\"agent_instance_id\\\"]` instead of the header.\",\n     \"In `migrations/001_init.sql` line 54, add the column `traceparent text` to `approvals.grants`. Store it in `request()` and restore it in `resume_with_approval`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_gateway_instance.py`. Send a call with a header that differs from the claim, and assert the claim is used.\",\n     \"Run the new test with `python -m pytest tests/test_gateway_instance.py`.\"],\n    \"The gateway uses the instance ID from the signed token. A header value cannot change which flag or rate limit applies.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"A05\", GW + AUD,\n    \"A stop flag for one agent type is not enforced at the gateway. Gateway audit rows keep IDs that the caller supplied.\",\n    [\"Do B04 first. It adds the `agent_type` stop scope and a signed `agent_type_id`.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, in `_log` at lines 137 to 139, replace the two `request.headers.get(...)` values with `c.get(\\\"agent_type_id\\\")` and the verified instance.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to rename the columns at `migrations/001_init.sql` line 23 to `agent_type_id` and `agent_instance_id`.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_gateway_stop.py`. It must pass.\",\n     \"In a test cluster, call the gateway with a spoofed header. Check the audit row holds the token's value.\"],\n    \"A flag with scope `agent_type` stops calls at the gateway, and its audit rows hold the signed type ID.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_gateway_stop.py\"))\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Configuration\nadd(\"C01\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The release manifest leaves out the issuers, audiences, MCP versions, tool fingerprints and cache settings. Most entries have no owner.\",\n    [\"In `release/manifest.yaml`, add to `identity_bindings` after line 71 the keys `sso: {issuer: https://sso.acme.example, audience: hr-helpdesk}` and `sts: {issuer: https://sts.acme.example, audience: hr-tool-gateway}`.\",\n     \"Add a key `mcp_protocol` under `tools` with the version the gateway speaks. Ask the gateway owner for it.\",\n     \"Under each server at lines 54 and 55, add `fingerprints: config/tools.yaml` and a `settings` key naming the retrieval cache ttl `cache_ttl_seconds: 900`.\",\n     \"For `system_prompt`, `configuration`, `network` and `admission`, add an `owner` and a `ref` with the git commit or file digest.\",\n     \"Run `python -c \\\"import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('release/manifest.yaml'))\\\"` to check the file still loads.\"],\n    \"`release/manifest.yaml` has issuer and audience for both token services and an owner for every entry.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"C02\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"One catch-all code owner can change the Dockerfile, dependencies and most of `src/` alone. No emergency change path is written down.\",\n    [\"In `CODEOWNERS`, insert three lines after line 1: `/src/`, `/Dockerfile` and `/requirements.txt`. Give each `@acme/people-platform @acme/security-engineering`.\",\n     \"Keep line 4 (`/src/gateway.py`) and line 5 below them, because the last matching line wins.\",\n     \"Create `docs/emergency-change.md`. Write who may approve an urgent change, how it is recorded, and when review happens after it.\",\n     \"Ask the repository admin to confirm that code-owner review is required on `main`.\",\n     \"Open a test pull request that changes `Dockerfile`. Check that GitHub asks for `@acme/security-engineering`.\"],\n    \"A pull request that changes `Dockerfile`, `requirements.txt` or `src/` needs the security team to review it.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"C03\", [\"agent\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\"],\n    \"Only the agent checks its own identity at start. Nothing outside it compares the running prompt, model and tools to the approved manifest.\",\n    [\"Create `k8s/identity-check.yaml` with a CronJob that runs every 15 minutes in `hr-agent`. Ask the platform team which image it should use.\",\n     \"Make the job read the `AGENT_TYPE_ID` of each running pod, and compare it to `agent_type_id` in the stored manifest for that release.\",\n     \"Make the job send an alert to the security channel and set a stop flag of scope `agent_type` when they differ.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to run the job against a test pod with a changed prompt. Check that the alert fires.\"],\n    \"A pod whose type ID differs from the approved manifest causes an alert within 15 minutes.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"C04\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No check compares the running prompts, tools, permissions and network rules with the approved baseline.\",\n    [\"Do C03 first. It adds the scheduled job.\",\n     \"Extend that job to hash the live `NetworkPolicy`, the `ClusterPolicy` and `tools.yaml` and compare them to hashes in `release/manifest.yaml`.\",\n     \"In `config/agent.yaml`, add a `drift` block with `alert_channel`, `response: stop_agent_type` and `max_minutes: 15`.\",\n     \"Change one network rule in a test cluster. Check that the alert and the response happen within 15 minutes.\"],\n    \"A changed network rule or tool file in a test cluster triggers an alert and a stop within 15 minutes.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"C05\", [\"model:claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\"],\n    \"Nothing re-tests the hosted model on a schedule or watches for provider notices.\",\n    [\"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, add a new workflow `.github/workflows/model-retest.yml` with `on: schedule` set to weekly.\",\n     \"Make the new workflow run `python -m pytest -q tests/release`, the same tests as the release.\",\n     \"Ask the model team to subscribe to the Anthropic model deprecation notices and name an owner in `release/manifest.yaml` under `models.primary`.\",\n     \"Trigger the workflow by hand once and check that it runs the tests.\"],\n    \"A weekly job runs the release tests against the pinned model, and a named person watches provider notices.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"C06\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"The release job runs tests in `tests/release`, but that folder does not exist. Results are not saved with the release.\",\n    [\"Create the folder `tests/release`. Create `tests/release/test_approval_text.py` from the test below, as a first case.\",\n     \"Add one test file for each of: denied destructive action, access limits, prompt injection, audit rows, stopping, retrieval and checkers.\",\n     \"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, change line 58 to a list of lines naming `type-id.json`, `release/manifest.yaml` and `test-results.xml`.\",\n     \"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, change line 29 to `python -m pytest -q tests/release --junitxml=test-results.xml`.\",\n     \"Ask the platform team to add a job after `build` that runs the same tests inside the built image digest.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/release`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The release job runs real tests and uploads `test-results.xml` with the manifest.\",\n    \"large\", {\"file\": \"tests/release/test_approval_text.py\", \"code\": (TRIAL / \"tests/test_approval_text.py\").read_text(),\n              \"run\": PYTEST + \"tests/release/test_approval_text.py\"})\n\nadd(\"C07\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"There is no stored earlier release, rollback steps or model retirement date.\",\n    [\"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, add a `rollback` job after line 75 that takes an old `git_sha` and re-applies its stored manifest.\",\n     \"Keep each release's manifest by digest. Ask the platform team where to store them.\",\n     \"In `release/manifest.yaml` under `models.primary`, add `retirement_date` from the provider notice. Ask the model team for it.\",\n     \"Create `docs/rollback.md` saying how to drain pending approvals and discard the cached index on rollback.\",\n     \"Run the rollback job once in a test cluster. Check that the older version answers a chat.\"],\n    \"A tested rollback job exists and the manifest holds the model retirement date.\",\n    \"large\")\n\nadd(\"C08\", GW + AUD,\n    \"Gateway rows cannot be tied to a stored release manifest, and audit rows are kept about six weeks instead of six months.\",\n    [\"Do E11 first. It fixes how long audit rows are kept.\",\n     \"Do A05 first. It stores a signed type ID in gateway rows.\",\n     \"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, upload the manifest under the name `manifest-<agent_type_id>` so it can be found by type ID.\",\n     \"In a test cluster, take one gateway row. Find its manifest using the stored type ID.\"],\n    \"From any gateway audit row you can find the exact release manifest by its type ID.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Ecosystem\nadd(\"E01\", [\"agent\", \"mcp:hr-tool-gateway\", \"api:sts\"],\n    \"No inventory covers the gateway, token service, registry, audit store and stop service. Entries have only one owner.\",\n    [\"In `release/manifest.yaml`, add a `services` list after line 55.\",\n     \"Add an entry for the gateway, STS, JWKS, image registry, Postgres and the telemetry collector.\",\n     \"Give each entry `agent_team_owner` and `provider_owner`.\",\n     \"Run `python -c \\\"import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('release/manifest.yaml'))\\\"` to check the file loads.\"],\n    \"Every outside service the agent uses has two named owners in `release/manifest.yaml`.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"E02\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No scan for known weaknesses runs in CI, and there are no records about who publishes each dependency.\",\n    [\"In `.github/workflows/release.yml`, add a step after line 28: `- run: pip install pip-audit && pip-audit -r requirements.txt --require-hashes`.\",\n     \"Create `docs/dependencies.md`. For each line in `requirements.txt`, write publisher, permissions and update source.\",\n     \"For `hris` and `helpdesk` in `config/tools.yaml`, add the publisher and update source next to `owner`.\",\n     \"Push a test branch. Check that the new step runs and the job fails when a known bad version is listed.\"],\n    \"The release job fails when a dependency has a known weakness, and every dependency has a record.\",\n    \"small\")\n\nadd(\"E03\", DR,\n    \"Tool fingerprints are checked only every 300 seconds, a list change message is ignored, and a gateway error skips the check.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, call `refresh_fingerprints()` before the tool lookup at line 165, with a short time limit. Refuse the call if it fails.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py` line 213, lower the sleep from 300 to 60 seconds.\",\n     \"In `config/tools.yaml`, add `implementation_ref` with the server's image digest under `hris` and `helpdesk`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_fingerprint.py` that changes a live description and asserts the tool is disabled. Run it.\"],\n    \"A changed tool description disables the tool before the next call and not after five minutes.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E04\", GW + [\"tool:search_policies\"],\n    \"Server instructions, descriptions and schemas are only fingerprinted. They are never scanned for hidden instructions.\",\n    [\"In `src/gateway.py`, add `scan_metadata(tool)` that rejects zero-width and control characters, long strings and phrases like `ignore previous`.\",\n     \"Call it from `refresh_fingerprints` at line 64 for every live tool, and disable the tool when it fails.\",\n     \"Also fetch `initialize` server `instructions` and scan them the same way.\",\n     \"Add a unit test with a description holding a zero-width character. Assert the tool is disabled.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_metadata_scan.py`.\"],\n    \"A tool with hidden characters or override words in its metadata is disabled before the model sees it.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E05\", GW,\n    \"Lookalike tool names across servers are only logged. Tricks such as Cyrillic letters are not detected.\",\n    [\"In `src/gateway.py`, replace the `log.error` at line 67 with `_disabled.update(...)` for every tool in the clash.\",\n     \"At line 65, add a confusables map for Cyrillic and Greek letters before the `casefold()` call.\",\n     \"In `src/approvals.py`, add the server id to the approval text in `describe()`.\",\n     \"Create `tests/test_lookalike.py` with the names `create_ticket` and `create_tіcket` (Cyrillic i). Assert both are disabled. Run it.\"],\n    \"Two tools whose names look alike are both disabled and the clash is logged.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E06\", DR,\n    \"When the gateway returns 503 the client sends `escalate_to_human` straight to the helpdesk server and skips the gateway.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Check `.mcp.json` and `src/gateway_client.py` for any other URL that is not `GATEWAY_URL`. There should be none.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_direct_route.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"The only network route to the helpdesk server goes through the gateway.\",\n    \"small\", test_of(\"test_direct_route.py\"))\n\nadd(\"E09\", DR + [\"api:sts\"],\n    \"A stop flag does not revoke tokens already issued. They last 300 seconds, and the direct route skips the stop check.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"In `src/credentials.py`, change line 20 from `300` to `60` so a stop is effective sooner.\",\n     \"In `src/credentials.py`, call `drop_subject` from `StopControl` when it cancels a run (`src/killswitch.py` line 58).\",\n     \"Ask the identity team for a revoke call. Call it for the subject when a stop flag appears.\",\n     \"In `src/agent.py`, record in-flight tool calls at stop. R13 adds this record.\",\n     \"Run `python -m pytest tests/test_audit_steps.py`. It must pass.\"],\n    \"After a stop, a copied token is refused within 60 seconds and every in-flight call has an audit row.\",\n    \"medium\", test_of(\"test_audit_steps.py\"))\n\nadd(\"E10\", GW + DR,\n    \"Gateway audit rows lack verified identity and the vendor's receipt ID, and an allow row is written only after the action.\",\n    [DO_B01,\n     \"Do A05 first. It stores a signed type ID in gateway rows.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, at line 190, add the `request_id` or `ticket_id` from `structured` to the reason written by `_log`.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, write a `pending` row before line 177 and update it after line 190. Return 503 if the first write fails.\",\n     \"Run a ticket call in a test cluster. Check the `audit.gateway_decisions` row holds the ticket id.\"],\n    \"Every gateway call has a row written before it runs and holds the vendor receipt ID after.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E11\", AUD,\n    \"Audit rows are kept about six weeks, not six months. Nothing shows if rows are missing or changed.\",\n    [\"In `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`, change line 35 from `\\\"6\\\"` to `\\\"27\\\"`. That is 26 weeks plus a spare.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team to add a `seq bigserial` column to `audit.events` and alert on gaps in it.\",\n     \"Ask them to export audit rows each day to storage that cannot be changed, and to alert if the export fails.\",\n     \"In `src/gateway.py`, write the audit row before forwarding the call. E10 covers this.\",\n     \"After the next night's run, ask the data-platform team to check that the oldest partition is about 26 weeks old.\"],\n    \"The oldest `audit.events` partition is at least 26 weeks old, and a gap in `seq` causes an alert.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\nadd(\"E12\", [\"agent\"],\n    \"No runbook, alert route, fleet impact query or outside-reporting owner is in the repository.\",\n    [\"Ask the security lead to write the runbook for an incident that affects every agent of this type, and create `docs/incident-runbook.md`.\",\n     \"Ask the data-platform team for a query that lists all runs and subjects touched by one agent type ID in a time range.\",\n     \"Name the person who decides on outside reporting in the runbook.\",\n     \"Run a drill: stop, quarantine and revoke the agent in a test cluster. Record the alert times in the runbook.\",\n     \"Check that `docs/incident-runbook.md` has the query, the owner, the alert times and the drill date.\"],\n    \"`docs/incident-runbook.md` holds a fleet impact query, a named reporting owner and a dated drill result.\",\n    \"medium\")\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\npath = AGENT / \"brace-findings.json\"\ndata = json.loads(path.read_text())\ncount = 0\nfor f in data[\"findings\"]:\n    if f[\"rating\"] in (\"gap\", \"needs_evidence\"):\n        entry = F.pop(f[\"item\"])\n        f[\"components\"] = entry[\"components\"]\n        f[\"fix\"] = entry[\"fix\"]\n        f[\"assignee\"] = None\n        count += 1\nassert not F, f\"unused fixes: {list(F)}\"\npath.write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\nprint(\"updated\", count)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RJmSYwKawMBKQ87TEiaZig","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
